               <fo:block space-before.optimum="5pt"
                         space-before.minimum="5pt"
                         space-before.maximum="5pt">The <fo:inline font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                             font-size="9pt"
                             letter-spacing="0.08em">Wire</fo:inline> object's scope must be calculated only once,
      when both the Producer and Consumer service become connected. When a
      Producer or Consumer service subsequently modifies its scope, the Wire
      object must <fo:inline font-style="italic">not</fo:inline> modify the original scope. A
      Consumer and a Produce service can thus assume that the scope does not
      change after the <fo:inline font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                             font-size="9pt"
                             letter-spacing="0.08em">producersConnected</fo:inline> method or
      <fo:inline font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                             font-size="9pt"
                             letter-spacing="0.08em">consumersConnected</fo:inline> method has been called.</fo:block>
            </fo:block>
            <fo:block id="d274e921">
               <fo:block>
                  <fo:block>
                     <fo:block keep-together.within-column="always"
                               margin-left="0pt"
                               font-family="ProductusSemibold,ArialUnicodeMS">
                        <fo:block keep-with-next.within-column="always">
                           <fo:block xmlns:d="http://docbook.org/ns/docbook"
                                     xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink"
                                     font-family="ProductusSemibold,ArialUnicodeMS"
                                     font-weight="normal"
                                     keep-with-next.within-column="always"
                                     space-before.minimum="0.8em"
                                     space-before.optimum="1.0em"
                                     space-before.maximum="1.2em"
                                     text-align="start"
                                     start-indent="0pt"
                                     hyphenate="false">
                              <fo:block font-size="12pt"
                                        line-height="14pt"
                                        space-before="8pt"
                                        space-after="5pt">
                                 <fo:list-block provisional-distance-between-starts="1in"
                                                provisional-label-separation="0.090in">
                                    <fo:list-item>
                                       <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()" text-align="start">
                                          <fo:block>108.6.3</fo:block>
                                       </fo:list-item-label>
                                       <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                                          <fo:block>Access Control</fo:block>
                                       </fo:list-item-body>
                                    </fo:list-item>
                                 </fo:list-block>
                              </fo:block>
                           </fo:block>
                        </fo:block>
                     </fo:block>
                  </fo:block>
               </fo:block>
               <fo:block space-before.optimum="5pt"
                         space-before.minimum="5pt"
                         space-before.maximum="5pt">When an <fo:inline font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                             font-size="9pt"
                             letter-spacing="0.08em">Envelope</fo:inline> object is used as argument in
      <fo:inline font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                             font-size="9pt"
                             letter-spacing="0.08em">Wire.update(Object)</fo:inline> then the <fo:inline font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                             font-size="9pt"
                             letter-spacing="0.08em">Wire</fo:inline> object must
      verify that the <fo:inline font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                             font-size="9pt"
                             letter-spacing="0.08em">Envelope</fo:inline> object's scope name is included in
      the <fo:inline font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                             font-size="9pt"
                             letter-spacing="0.08em">Wire</fo:inline> object's scope. If this is not the case, the
      update must be ignored (the <fo:inline font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                             font-size="9pt"
                             letter-spacing="0.08em">updated</fo:inline> method on the Consumer
      service must not be called).</fo:block>
               <fo:block space-before.optimum="5pt"
                         space-before.minimum="5pt"
                         space-before.maximum="5pt">A composite Producer represents a number of values, which is
      different from a normal Producer that can always return a single object
      from the <fo:inline font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                             font-size="9pt"
                             letter-spacing="0.08em">poll</fo:inline> method. A composite Producer must therefore
      return an array of <fo:inline font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                             font-size="9pt"
                             letter-spacing="0.08em">Envelope</fo:inline> objects
      (<fo:inline font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                             font-size="9pt"
                             letter-spacing="0.08em">Envelope[]</fo:inline>). This array must contain <fo:inline font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                             font-size="9pt"
                             letter-spacing="0.08em">Envelope</fo:inline>
      objects for all the values that are in the <fo:inline font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                             font-size="9pt"
                             letter-spacing="0.08em">Wire</fo:inline> object's
      scope. It is permitted to return all possible values for the Producer
      because the <fo:inline font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                             font-size="9pt"
                             letter-spacing="0.08em">Wire</fo:inline> object must remove all
      <fo:inline font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                             font-size="9pt"
                             letter-spacing="0.08em">Envelope</fo:inline> objects that have a scope name not listed in the
      <fo:inline font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                             font-size="9pt"
                             letter-spacing="0.08em">Wire</fo:inline> object's scope.</fo:block>
            </fo:block>
            <fo:block id="d274e957">
               <fo:block>
                  <fo:block>
                     <fo:block keep-together.within-column="always"
                               margin-left="0pt"
                               font-family="ProductusSemibold,ArialUnicodeMS">
                        <fo:block keep-with-next.within-column="always">
                           <fo:block xmlns:d="http://docbook.org/ns/docbook"
                                     xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink"
                                     font-family="ProductusSemibold,ArialUnicodeMS"
                                     font-weight="normal"
                                     keep-with-next.within-column="always"
                                     space-before.minimum="0.8em"
                                     space-before.optimum="1.0em"
                                     space-before.maximum="1.2em"
                                     text-align="start"
                                     start-indent="0pt"
                                     hyphenate="false">
                              <fo:block font-size="12pt"
                                        line-height="14pt"
                                        space-before="8pt"
                                        space-after="5pt">
                                 <fo:list-block provisional-distance-between-starts="1in"
                                                provisional-label-separation="0.090in">
                                    <fo:list-item>
                                       <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()" text-align="start">
                                          <fo:block>108.6.4</fo:block>
                                       </fo:list-item-label>
                                       <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                                          <fo:block>Composites and Flavors</fo:block>
                                       </fo:list-item-body>
                                    </fo:list-item>
                                 </fo:list-block>
                              </fo:block>
                           </fo:block>
                        </fo:block>
                     </fo:block>
                  </fo:block>
               </fo:block>
               <fo:block space-before.optimum="5pt"
                         space-before.minimum="5pt"
                         space-before.maximum="5pt">Composite Producer and Consumer services must always use a flavor
      of the <fo:inline font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                             font-size="9pt"
                             letter-spacing="0.08em">Envelope</fo:inline> class. The data types of the values must be
      associated with the scope name or identification and mutually agreed
      between the Consumer and Producer services.</fo:block>
               <fo:block space-before.optimum="5pt"
                         space-before.minimum="5pt"
                         space-before.maximum="5pt">Flavors and <fo:inline font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                             font-size="9pt"
                             letter-spacing="0.08em">Envelope</fo:inline> objects both represent
      categories of different values. Flavors, however, are different Java
      classes that represent the same kind of value. For example, the tire
      pressure of the left front wheel could be passed as a
      <fo:inline font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                             font-size="9pt"
                             letter-spacing="0.08em">Float</fo:inline>, an <fo:inline font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                             font-size="9pt"
                             letter-spacing="0.08em">Integer</fo:inline>, or a
      <fo:inline font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                             font-size="9pt"
                             letter-spacing="0.08em">Measurement</fo:inline> object. Whatever data type is chosen, it is
      still the tire pressure of the left front wheel. The
      <fo:inline font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                             font-size="9pt"
                             letter-spacing="0.08em">Envelope</fo:inline> object represents the kind of object, for example
      the right front wheel tire pressure, or the left rear wheel.</fo:block>
            </fo:block>
            <fo:block id="i1425603">
               <fo:block>
                  <fo:block>
                     <fo:block keep-together.within-column="always"
                               margin-left="0pt"
                               font-family="ProductusSemibold,ArialUnicodeMS">
                        <fo:block keep-with-next.within-column="always">
                           <fo:block xmlns:d="http://docbook.org/ns/docbook"
                                     xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink"
                                     font-family="ProductusSemibold,ArialUnicodeMS"
                                     font-weight="normal"
                                     keep-with-next.within-column="always"
                                     space-before.minimum="0.8em"
                                     space-before.optimum="1.0em"
                                     space-before.maximum="1.2em"
                                     text-align="start"
                                     start-indent="0pt"
                                     hyphenate="false">
                              <fo:block font-size="12pt"
                                        line-height="14pt"
                                        space-before="8pt"
                                        space-after="5pt">
                                 <fo:list-block provisional-distance-between-starts="1in"
                                                provisional-label-separation="0.090in">
                                    <fo:list-item>
                                       <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()" text-align="start">
                                          <fo:block>108.6.5</fo:block>
                                       </fo:list-item-label>
                                       <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                                          <fo:block>Scope name syntax</fo:block>
                                       </fo:list-item-body>
                                    </fo:list-item>
                                 </fo:list-block>
                              </fo:block>
                           </fo:block>
                        </fo:block>
                     </fo:block>
                  </fo:block>
               </fo:block>
               <fo:block space-before.optimum="5pt"
                         space-before.minimum="5pt"
                         space-before.maximum="5pt">Scope names are normal <fo:inline font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                             font-size="9pt"
                             letter-spacing="0.08em">String</fo:inline> objects and can, in
      principle, contain any Unicode character. In use, scope names can be a
      full wildcard ('*') but they cannot be partially wildcarded for matching
      scopes.</fo:block>
               <fo:block space-before.optimum="5pt"
                         space-before.minimum="5pt"
                         space-before.maximum="5pt">Scope names are used with the <fo:inline font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                             font-size="9pt"
                             letter-spacing="0.08em">WirePermission</fo:inline> class
      that extends <fo:inline font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                             font-size="9pt"
                             letter-spacing="0.08em">java.security.BasicPermission</fo:inline>. The
      <fo:inline font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                             font-size="9pt"
                             letter-spacing="0.08em">BasicPermission</fo:inline> class implements the <fo:inline font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                             font-size="9pt"
                             letter-spacing="0.08em">implies</fo:inline>
      method and performs the name matching. The wildcard matching of this
      class is based on the concept of names where the constituents of the
      name are separated with a period (<fo:inline font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                             font-size="9pt"
                             letter-spacing="0.08em">'.'</fo:inline>): for example,
      <fo:inline font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                             font-size="9pt"
                             letter-spacing="0.08em">org.osgi.service.http.port</fo:inline>.</fo:block>
               <fo:block space-before.optimum="5pt"
                         space-before.minimum="5pt"
                         space-before.maximum="5pt">Scope names must therefore follow the rules for fully qualified
      Java class names. For example, <fo:inline font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                             font-size="9pt"
                             letter-spacing="0.08em">door.lock</fo:inline> is a correct scope
      name while <fo:inline font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                             font-size="9pt"
                             letter-spacing="0.08em">door-lock</fo:inline> is not.</fo:block>
            </fo:block>
         </fo:block>
         <fo:block id="i1456291">
            <fo:block>
               <fo:block>
                  <fo:block keep-together.within-column="always"
                            margin-left="0pt"
                            font-family="ProductusSemibold,ArialUnicodeMS">
                     <fo:block keep-with-next.within-column="always">
                        <fo:block xmlns:d="http://docbook.org/ns/docbook"
                                  xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink"
                                  font-family="ProductusSemibold,ArialUnicodeMS"
                                  font-weight="normal"
                                  keep-with-next.within-column="always"
                                  space-before.minimum="0.8em"
                                  space-before.optimum="1.0em"
                                  space-before.maximum="1.2em"
                                  text-align="start"
                                  start-indent="0pt"
                                  hyphenate="false">
                           <fo:marker marker-class-name="section.head.marker">Wire Flow Control</fo:marker>
                           <fo:block font-size="18pt"
                                     line-height="25pt"
                                     space-before="12.5pt"
                                     space-after="12pt">
                              <fo:list-block provisional-distance-between-starts="1in"
                                             provisional-label-separation="0.090in">
                                 <fo:list-item>
                                    <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()" text-align="start">
                                       <fo:block>108.7</fo:block>
                                    </fo:list-item-label>
                                    <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                                       <fo:block>Wire Flow Control</fo:block>
                                    </fo:list-item-body>
                                 </fo:list-item>
                              </fo:list-block>
                           </fo:block>
                        </fo:block>
                     </fo:block>
                  </fo:block>
               </fo:block>
            </fo:block>
            <fo:block space-before.optimum="5pt"
                      space-before.minimum="5pt"
                      space-before.maximum="5pt">The <fo:inline font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                          font-size="9pt"
                          letter-spacing="0.08em">WIREADMIN_FILTER</fo:inline> property contains a filter
    expression (as defined in the OSGi Framework <fo:inline font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                          font-size="9pt"
                          letter-spacing="0.08em">Filter</fo:inline> class)
    that is used to limit the number of updates to the <fo:inline font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                          font-size="9pt"
                          letter-spacing="0.08em">Consumer</fo:inline>
    service. This is necessary because information can arrive at a much
    greater rate than can be processed by a <fo:inline font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                          font-size="9pt"
                          letter-spacing="0.08em">Consumer</fo:inline> service. For
    example, a single CAN bus (the electronic control bus used in current
    cars) in a car can easily deliver hundreds of measurements per second to
    an OSGi based controller. Most of these measurements are not relevant to
    the OSGi bundles, at least not all the time. For example, a bundle that
    maintains an indicator for the presence of frost is only interested in
    measurements when the outside temperature passes the 4 degrees Celsius
    mark.</fo:block>
            <fo:block space-before.optimum="5pt"
                      space-before.minimum="5pt"
                      space-before.maximum="5pt">Limiting the number of updates from a Producer service can make a
    significant difference in performance (meaning that less hardware is
    needed). For example, a vendor can implement the filter in native code and
    remove unnecessary updates prior to processing in the Java Virtual Machine
    (JVM). This is depicted in <fo:basic-link xmlns:d="http://docbook.org/ns/docbook"
                              xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink"
                              internal-destination="i1300018">
                  <fo:inline color="inherit"
                             font-family="inherit"
                             letter-spacing="inherit"
                             hyphenate="inherit">Figure 108.5 on page <fo:page-number-citation ref-id="i1300018"/>
                  </fo:inline>
               </fo:basic-link>.</fo:block>
            <fo:block start-indent="0pt">
               <fo:block space-before.minimum="0.5em"
                         space-before.optimum="1em"
                         space-before.maximum="2em"
                         space-after.minimum="0.5em"
                         space-after.optimum="1em"
                         space-after.maximum="2em"
                         keep-together.within-column="always"
                         id="i1300018">
                  <fo:block xmlns:d="http://docbook.org/ns/docbook"
                            xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink"
                            space-before.optimum="5pt"
                            space-before.minimum="5pt"
                            space-before.maximum="5pt"
                            font-weight="normal"
                            font-size="9pt"
                            hyphenate="false"
                            space-after.minimum="0.4em"
                            space-after.optimum="0.6em"
                            space-after.maximum="0.8em"
                            start-indent="0pt"
                            font-family="Proforma-Book,ArialUnicodeMS"
                            font-style="italic"
                            keep-with-next.within-column="always">
                     <fo:list-block provisional-distance-between-starts="1in"
                                    provisional-label-separation="0.090in">
                        <fo:list-item>
                           <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()" text-align="start">
                              <fo:block>Figure 108.5</fo:block>
                           </fo:list-item-label>
                           <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                              <fo:block>Filtering of Updates</fo:block>
                           </fo:list-item-body>
                        </fo:list-item>
                     </fo:list-block>
                  </fo:block>
                  <fo:block id="d274e1020" text-align="center">
                     <fo:external-graphic src="url(file:///home/stbischof/git/OSGI_MIGRATE/osgi_target/org.osgi.service.wireadmin/spec/org.osgi.spec.service.wireadmin/src/main/resources/spec/update-filtering.svg)"
                                          width="auto"
                                          height="auto"
                                          content-width="7.000in"
                                          content-height="2.100in"
                                          text-align="center"/>
                  </fo:block>
               </fo:block>
            </fo:block>
            <fo:block space-before.optimum="5pt"
                      space-before.minimum="5pt"
                      space-before.maximum="5pt">The filter can use any combination of the following attributes in a
    filter to implement many common filtering schemes:</fo:block>
            <fo:block xmlns:rx="http://www.renderx.com/XSL/Extensions"
                      space-before.minimum="0.5em"
                      space-before.optimum="1em"
                      space-before.maximum="2em"
                      space-after.minimum="0.5em"
                      space-after.optimum="1em"
                      space-after.maximum="2em"
                      keep-together.within-column="auto"
                      id="d274e1024">
               <fo:block xmlns:d="http://docbook.org/ns/docbook"
                         xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink"
                         space-before.optimum="5pt"
                         space-before.minimum="5pt"
                         space-before.maximum="5pt"
                         font-weight="normal"
                         font-size="9pt"
                         hyphenate="false"
                         space-after.minimum="0.4em"
                         space-after.optimum="0.6em"
                         space-after.maximum="0.8em"
                         start-indent="0pt"
                         font-family="Proforma-Book,ArialUnicodeMS"
                         font-style="italic"
                         keep-with-next.within-column="always">
                  <fo:list-block provisional-distance-between-starts="1in"
                                 provisional-label-separation="0.090in">
                     <fo:list-item>
                        <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()" text-align="start">
                           <fo:block>Table 108.3</fo:block>
                        </fo:list-item-label>
                        <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                           <fo:block>Filter Attribute Names</fo:block>
                        </fo:list-item-body>
                     </fo:list-item>
                  </fo:list-block>
               </fo:block>
               <fo:table border-before-width.conditionality="retain"
                         border-collapse="collapse"
                         table-layout="fixed"
                         width="100%">
                  <fo:table-column column-number="1" column-width="proportional-column-width(2)"/>
                  <fo:table-column column-number="2" column-width="proportional-column-width(3)"/>
                  <fo:table-header start-indent="0pt" end-indent="0pt">
                     <fo:table-row keep-together.within-column="always"
                                   keep-with-next.within-column="always"
                                   font-family="ProductusSemibold,ArialUnicodeMS">
                        <fo:table-cell padding-start="0pt"
                                       padding-end="4pt"
                                       padding-top="1pt"
                                       padding-bottom="1pt">
                           <fo:block>Constant</fo:block>
                        </fo:table-cell>
                        <fo:table-cell padding-start="0pt"
                                       padding-end="4pt"
                                       padding-top="1pt"
                                       padding-bottom="1pt">
                           <fo:block>Description</fo:block>
                        </fo:table-cell>
                     </fo:table-row>
                  </fo:table-header>
                  <fo:table-body start-indent="0pt" end-indent="0pt">
                     <fo:table-row keep-together.within-column="always">
                        <fo:table-cell padding-start="0pt"
                                       padding-end="4pt"
                                       padding-top="1pt"
                                       padding-bottom="1pt">
                           <fo:block>
                              <fo:inline font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                                         font-size="9pt"
                                         letter-spacing="0.08em">WIREVALUE_CURRENT</fo:inline>
                           </fo:block>
                        </fo:table-cell>
                        <fo:table-cell padding-start="0pt"
                                       padding-end="4pt"
                                       padding-top="1pt"
                                       padding-bottom="1pt">
                           <fo:block>
                              <fo:block space-before.optimum="5pt"
                                        space-before.minimum="5pt"
                                        space-before.maximum="5pt">Current value of the data from the Producer
            service.</fo:block>
                           </fo:block>
                        </fo:table-cell>
                     </fo:table-row>
                     <fo:table-row keep-together.within-column="always">
                        <fo:table-cell padding-start="0pt"
                                       padding-end="4pt"
                                       padding-top="1pt"
                                       padding-bottom="1pt">
                           <fo:block>
                              <fo:inline font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                                         font-size="9pt"
                                         letter-spacing="0.08em">WIREVALUE_PREVIOUS</fo:inline>
                           </fo:block>
                        </fo:table-cell>
                        <fo:table-cell padding-start="0pt"
                                       padding-end="4pt"
                                       padding-top="1pt"
                                       padding-bottom="1pt">
                           <fo:block>
                              <fo:block space-before.optimum="5pt"
                                        space-before.minimum="5pt"
                                        space-before.maximum="5pt">Previous data value that was reported to the Consumer
            service.</fo:block>
                           </fo:block>
                        </fo:table-cell>
                     </fo:table-row>
                     <fo:table-row keep-together.within-column="always">
                        <fo:table-cell padding-start="0pt"
                                       padding-end="4pt"
                                       padding-top="1pt"
                                       padding-bottom="1pt">
                           <fo:block>
                              <fo:inline font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                                         font-size="9pt"
                                         letter-spacing="0.08em">WIREVALUE_DELTA_ABSOLUTE</fo:inline>
                           </fo:block>
                        </fo:table-cell>
                        <fo:table-cell padding-start="0pt"
                                       padding-end="4pt"
                                       padding-top="1pt"
                                       padding-bottom="1pt">
                           <fo:block>
                              <fo:block space-before.optimum="5pt"
                                        space-before.minimum="5pt"
                                        space-before.maximum="5pt">The actual positive difference between the previous
            data value and the current data value. For example, if the
            previous data value was 3 and the current data value is -0.5, then
            the absolute delta is 3.5. This filter attribute is not set when
            the current or previous value is not a number.</fo:block>
                           </fo:block>
                        </fo:table-cell>
                     </fo:table-row>
                     <fo:table-row keep-together.within-column="always">
                        <fo:table-cell padding-start="0pt"
                                       padding-end="4pt"
                                       padding-top="1pt"
                                       padding-bottom="1pt">
                           <fo:block>
                              <fo:inline font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                                         font-size="9pt"
                                         letter-spacing="0.08em">WIREVALUE_DELTA_RELATIVE</fo:inline>
                           </fo:block>
                        </fo:table-cell>
                        <fo:table-cell padding-start="0pt"
                                       padding-end="4pt"
                                       padding-top="1pt"
                                       padding-bottom="1pt">
                           <fo:block>
                              <fo:block space-before.optimum="5pt"
                                        space-before.minimum="5pt"
                                        space-before.maximum="5pt">The absolute (meaning always positive) relative
            change between the current and the previous data values,
            calculated with the following formula:<fo:inline font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                                            font-size="9pt"
                                            letter-spacing="0.08em">
            |previous-current|/|current|</fo:inline>. For example, if the previous
            value was 3 and the new value is 5, then the relative delta is
            <fo:inline font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                                            font-size="9pt"
                                            letter-spacing="0.08em">|3-5|/|5| = 0.4</fo:inline>. This filter attribute is not set
            when the current or previous value is not a number.</fo:block>
                           </fo:block>
                        </fo:table-cell>
                     </fo:table-row>
                     <fo:table-row keep-together.within-column="always">
                        <fo:table-cell padding-start="0pt"
                                       padding-end="4pt"
                                       padding-top="1pt"
                                       padding-bottom="1pt">
                           <fo:block>
                              <fo:inline font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                                         font-size="9pt"
                                         letter-spacing="0.08em">WIREVALUE_ELAPSED</fo:inline>
                           </fo:block>
                        </fo:table-cell>
                        <fo:table-cell padding-start="0pt"
                                       padding-end="4pt"
                                       padding-top="1pt"
                                       padding-bottom="1pt">
                           <fo:block>
                              <fo:block space-before.optimum="5pt"
                                        space-before.minimum="5pt"
                                        space-before.maximum="5pt">The time in milliseconds between the last time the
            <fo:inline font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                                            font-size="9pt"
                                            letter-spacing="0.08em">Consumer</fo:inline>. <fo:basic-link xmlns:d="http://docbook.org/ns/docbook"
                                                xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink"
                                                internal-destination="org.osgi.service.wireadmin.Consumer.updated-Wire-Object-">
                                    <fo:inline color="blue"
                                               font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                                               letter-spacing="0.08em"
                                               hyphenate="false">updated(Wire,Object)</fo:inline>
                                 </fo:basic-link> returned and the time the filter is
            evaluated.</fo:block>
                           </fo:block>
                        </fo:table-cell>
                     </fo:table-row>
                  </fo:table-body>
               </fo:table>
            </fo:block>
            <fo:block space-before.optimum="5pt"
                      space-before.minimum="5pt"
                      space-before.maximum="5pt">Filter attributes can be used to implement many common filtering
    schemes that limit the number of updates that are sent to a Consumer
    service. The Wire Admin service specification requires that updates to a
    Consumer service are always filtered if the <fo:inline font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                          font-size="9pt"
                          letter-spacing="0.08em">WIREADMIN_FILTER</fo:inline>
    Wire property is present. Producer services that wish to perform the
    filtering themselves should register with a service property
    <fo:inline font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                          font-size="9pt"
                          letter-spacing="0.08em">WIREADMIN_PRODUCER_FILTERS</fo:inline>. Filtering must be performed by
    the <fo:inline font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                          font-size="9pt"
                          letter-spacing="0.08em">Wire</fo:inline> object for all other Producer services.</fo:block>
            <fo:block space-before.optimum="5pt"
                      space-before.minimum="5pt"
                      space-before.maximum="5pt">Filtering for composite Producer services is not supported. When a
    filter is set on a <fo:inline font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                          font-size="9pt"
                          letter-spacing="0.08em">Wire</fo:inline> object, the Wire must still perform
    the filtering (which is limited to time filtering because an
    <fo:inline font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                          font-size="9pt"
                          letter-spacing="0.08em">Envelope</fo:inline> object is not a magnitude), but this approach may
    lose relevant information because the objects are of a different kind. For
    example, an update of every 500 ms could miss all speed updates because
    there is a wheel pressure update that resets the elapsed time. Producer
    services should, however, still implement a filtering scheme that could
    use proprietary attributes to filter on different kind of objects.</fo:block>
            <fo:block id="d274e1083">
               <fo:block>
                  <fo:block>
                     <fo:block keep-together.within-column="always"
                               margin-left="0pt"
                               font-family="ProductusSemibold,ArialUnicodeMS">
                        <fo:block keep-with-next.within-column="always">
                           <fo:block xmlns:d="http://docbook.org/ns/docbook"
                                     xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink"
                                     font-family="ProductusSemibold,ArialUnicodeMS"
                                     font-weight="normal"
                                     keep-with-next.within-column="always"
                                     space-before.minimum="0.8em"
                                     space-before.optimum="1.0em"
                                     space-before.maximum="1.2em"
                                     text-align="start"
                                     start-indent="0pt"
                                     hyphenate="false">
                              <fo:block font-size="12pt"
                                        line-height="14pt"
                                        space-before="8pt"
                                        space-after="5pt">
                                 <fo:list-block provisional-distance-between-starts="1in"
                                                provisional-label-separation="0.090in">
                                    <fo:list-item>
                                       <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()" text-align="start">
                                          <fo:block>108.7.1</fo:block>
                                       </fo:list-item-label>
                                       <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                                          <fo:block>Filtering by Time</fo:block>
                                       </fo:list-item-body>
                                    </fo:list-item>
                                 </fo:list-block>
                              </fo:block>
                           </fo:block>
                        </fo:block>
                     </fo:block>
                  </fo:block>
               </fo:block>
               <fo:block space-before.optimum="5pt"
                         space-before.minimum="5pt"
                         space-before.maximum="5pt">The simplest filter mechanism is based on time. The
      <fo:inline font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                             font-size="9pt"
                             letter-spacing="0.08em">wirevalue.elapsed</fo:inline> attribute contains the amount of
      milliseconds that have passed since the last update to the associated
      <fo:inline font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                             font-size="9pt"
                             letter-spacing="0.08em">Consumer</fo:inline> service. The following example filter expression
      illustrates how the updates can be limited to approximately 40 times per
      minute (once every 1500 ms).</fo:block>
               <fo:block space-before.minimum="0.8em"
                         space-before.optimum="1em"
                         space-before.maximum="1.2em"
                         space-after.minimum="0.8em"
                         space-after.optimum="1em"
                         space-after.maximum="1.2em"
                         hyphenate="false"
                         wrap-option="no-wrap"
                         white-space-collapse="false"
                         white-space-treatment="preserve"
                         linefeed-treatment="preserve"
                         text-align="start"
                         font-family="ProductusOSGiMonoc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                         font-size="9pt"
                         letter-spacing="-.0em"
                         space-before="5pt"
                         space-after="3pt"
                         space-after.conditionality="retain"
                         start-indent="inherit"
                         line-height="11pt"
                         id="d274e1091">(wirevalue.elapsed&gt;=1500)</fo:block>
               <fo:block space-before.optimum="5pt"
                         space-before.minimum="5pt"
                         space-before.maximum="5pt">
                  <fo:basic-link xmlns:d="http://docbook.org/ns/docbook"
                                 xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink"
                                 internal-destination="i1286742">
                     <fo:inline color="inherit"
                                font-family="inherit"
                                letter-spacing="inherit"
                                hyphenate="inherit">Figure 108.6</fo:inline>
                  </fo:basic-link> depicts this example
      graphically.</fo:block>
               <fo:block space-before.minimum="0.5em"
                         space-before.optimum="1em"
                         space-before.maximum="2em"
                         space-after.minimum="0.5em"
                         space-after.optimum="1em"
                         space-after.maximum="2em"
                         keep-together.within-column="always"
                         id="i1286742">
                  <fo:block xmlns:d="http://docbook.org/ns/docbook"
                            xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink"
                            space-before.optimum="5pt"
                            space-before.minimum="5pt"
                            space-before.maximum="5pt"
                            font-weight="normal"
                            font-size="9pt"
                            hyphenate="false"
                            space-after.minimum="0.4em"
                            space-after.optimum="0.6em"
                            space-after.maximum="0.8em"
                            start-indent="0pt"
                            font-family="Proforma-Book,ArialUnicodeMS"
                            font-style="italic"
                            keep-with-next.within-column="always">
                     <fo:list-block provisional-distance-between-starts="1in"
                                    provisional-label-separation="0.090in">
                        <fo:list-item>
                           <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()" text-align="start">
                              <fo:block>Figure 108.6</fo:block>
                           </fo:list-item-label>
                           <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                              <fo:block>Elapsed Time Change</fo:block>
                           </fo:list-item-body>
                        </fo:list-item>
                     </fo:list-block>
                  </fo:block>
                  <fo:block id="d274e1097" text-align="center">
                     <fo:external-graphic src="url(file:///home/stbischof/git/OSGI_MIGRATE/osgi_target/org.osgi.service.wireadmin/spec/org.osgi.spec.service.wireadmin/src/main/resources/spec/elapsed-time-change.svg)"
                                          width="auto"
                                          height="auto"
                                          content-width="7.000in"
                                          content-height="1.500in"
                                          text-align="center"/>
                  </fo:block>
               </fo:block>
            </fo:block>
            <fo:block id="d274e1100">
               <fo:block>
                  <fo:block>
                     <fo:block keep-together.within-column="always"
                               margin-left="0pt"
                               font-family="ProductusSemibold,ArialUnicodeMS">
                        <fo:block keep-with-next.within-column="always">
                           <fo:block xmlns:d="http://docbook.org/ns/docbook"
                                     xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink"
                                     font-family="ProductusSemibold,ArialUnicodeMS"
                                     font-weight="normal"
                                     keep-with-next.within-column="always"
                                     space-before.minimum="0.8em"
                                     space-before.optimum="1.0em"
                                     space-before.maximum="1.2em"
                                     text-align="start"
                                     start-indent="0pt"
                                     hyphenate="false">
                              <fo:block font-size="12pt"
                                        line-height="14pt"
                                        space-before="8pt"
                                        space-after="5pt">
                                 <fo:list-block provisional-distance-between-starts="1in"
                                                provisional-label-separation="0.090in">
                                    <fo:list-item>
                                       <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()" text-align="start">
                                          <fo:block>108.7.2</fo:block>
                                       </fo:list-item-label>
                                       <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                                          <fo:block>Filtering by Change</fo:block>
                                       </fo:list-item-body>
                                    </fo:list-item>
                                 </fo:list-block>
                              </fo:block>
                           </fo:block>
                        </fo:block>
                     </fo:block>
                  </fo:block>
               </fo:block>
               <fo:block space-before.optimum="5pt"
                         space-before.minimum="5pt"
                         space-before.maximum="5pt">A Consumer service is often not interested in an update if the
      data value has not changed. The following filter expression shows how a
      Consumer service can limit the updates from a temperature sensor to be
      sent only when the temperature has changed at least 1 °K.</fo:block>
               <fo:block space-before.minimum="0.8em"
                         space-before.optimum="1em"
                         space-before.maximum="1.2em"
                         space-after.minimum="0.8em"
                         space-after.optimum="1em"
                         space-after.maximum="1.2em"
                         hyphenate="false"
                         wrap-option="no-wrap"
                         white-space-collapse="false"
                         white-space-treatment="preserve"
                         linefeed-treatment="preserve"
                         text-align="start"
                         font-family="ProductusOSGiMonoc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                         font-size="9pt"
                         letter-spacing="-.0em"
                         space-before="5pt"
                         space-after="3pt"
                         space-after.conditionality="retain"
                         start-indent="inherit"
                         line-height="11pt"
                         id="d274e1103">(wirevalue.delta.absolute&gt;=1)</fo:block>
               <fo:block space-before.optimum="5pt"
                         space-before.minimum="5pt"
                         space-before.maximum="5pt">
                  <fo:basic-link xmlns:d="http://docbook.org/ns/docbook"
                                 xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink"
                                 internal-destination="i1274545">
                     <fo:inline color="inherit"
                                font-family="inherit"
                                letter-spacing="inherit"
                                hyphenate="inherit">Figure 108.7</fo:inline>
                  </fo:basic-link> depicts a band that is created by the
      absolute delta between the previous data value and the current data
      value. The Consumer is only notified with the <fo:basic-link xmlns:d="http://docbook.org/ns/docbook"
                                 xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink"
                                 internal-destination="org.osgi.service.wireadmin.Consumer.updated-Wire-Object-">
                     <fo:inline color="blue"
                                font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                                letter-spacing="0.08em"
                                hyphenate="false">updated(Wire,Object)</fo:inline>
                  </fo:basic-link> method when a data value is outside of this
      band.</fo:block>
               <fo:block space-before.minimum="0.5em"
                         space-before.optimum="1em"
                         space-before.maximum="2em"
                         space-after.minimum="0.5em"
                         space-after.optimum="1em"
                         space-after.maximum="2em"
                         keep-together.within-column="always"
                         id="i1274545">
                  <fo:block xmlns:d="http://docbook.org/ns/docbook"
                            xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink"
                            space-before.optimum="5pt"
                            space-before.minimum="5pt"
                            space-before.maximum="5pt"
                            font-weight="normal"
                            font-size="9pt"
                            hyphenate="false"
                            space-after.minimum="0.4em"
                            space-after.optimum="0.6em"
                            space-after.maximum="0.8em"
                            start-indent="0pt"
                            font-family="Proforma-Book,ArialUnicodeMS"
                            font-style="italic"
                            keep-with-next.within-column="always">
                     <fo:list-block provisional-distance-between-starts="1in"
                                    provisional-label-separation="0.090in">
                        <fo:list-item>
                           <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()" text-align="start">
                              <fo:block>Figure 108.7</fo:block>
                           </fo:list-item-label>
                           <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                              <fo:block>Absolute Delta</fo:block>
                           </fo:list-item-body>
                        </fo:list-item>
                     </fo:list-block>
                  </fo:block>
                  <fo:block id="d274e1111" text-align="center">
                     <fo:external-graphic src="url(file:///home/stbischof/git/OSGI_MIGRATE/osgi_target/org.osgi.service.wireadmin/spec/org.osgi.spec.service.wireadmin/src/main/resources/spec/absolute-delta.svg)"
                                          width="auto"
                                          height="auto"
                                          content-width="7.000in"
                                          content-height="1.294in"
                                          text-align="center"/>
                  </fo:block>
               </fo:block>
               <fo:block space-before.optimum="5pt"
                         space-before.minimum="5pt"
                         space-before.maximum="5pt">The delta may also be relative. For example, if a car is moving
      slowly, then updates for the speed of the car are interesting even for
      small variations. When a car is moving at a high rate of speed, updates
      are only interesting for larger variations in speed. The following
      example shows how the updates can be limited to data value changes of at
      least 10%.</fo:block>
               <fo:block space-before.minimum="0.8em"
                         space-before.optimum="1em"
                         space-before.maximum="1.2em"
                         space-after.minimum="0.8em"
                         space-after.optimum="1em"
                         space-after.maximum="1.2em"
                         hyphenate="false"
                         wrap-option="no-wrap"
                         white-space-collapse="false"
                         white-space-treatment="preserve"
                         linefeed-treatment="preserve"
                         text-align="start"
                         font-family="ProductusOSGiMonoc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                         font-size="9pt"
                         letter-spacing="-.0em"
                         space-before="5pt"
                         space-after="3pt"
                         space-after.conditionality="retain"
                         start-indent="inherit"
                         line-height="11pt"
                         id="d274e1115">(wirevalue.delta.relative&gt;=0.1)</fo:block>
               <fo:block space-before.optimum="5pt"
                         space-before.minimum="5pt"
                         space-before.maximum="5pt">
                  <fo:basic-link xmlns:d="http://docbook.org/ns/docbook"
                                 xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink"
                                 internal-destination="i1274674">
                     <fo:inline color="inherit"
                                font-family="inherit"
                                letter-spacing="inherit"
                                hyphenate="inherit">Figure 108.8 on page <fo:page-number-citation ref-id="i1274674"/>
                     </fo:inline>
                  </fo:basic-link> depicts a relative band.
      Notice that the size of the band is directly proportional to the size of
      the sample value.</fo:block>
               <fo:block space-before.minimum="0.5em"
                         space-before.optimum="1em"
                         space-before.maximum="2em"
                         space-after.minimum="0.5em"
                         space-after.optimum="1em"
                         space-after.maximum="2em"
                         keep-together.within-column="always"
                         id="i1274674">
                  <fo:block xmlns:d="http://docbook.org/ns/docbook"
                            xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink"
                            space-before.optimum="5pt"
                            space-before.minimum="5pt"
                            space-before.maximum="5pt"
                            font-weight="normal"
                            font-size="9pt"
                            hyphenate="false"
                            space-after.minimum="0.4em"
                            space-after.optimum="0.6em"
                            space-after.maximum="0.8em"
                            start-indent="0pt"
                            font-family="Proforma-Book,ArialUnicodeMS"
                            font-style="italic"
                            keep-with-next.within-column="always">
                     <fo:list-block provisional-distance-between-starts="1in"
                                    provisional-label-separation="0.090in">
                        <fo:list-item>
                           <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()" text-align="start">
                              <fo:block>Figure 108.8</fo:block>
                           </fo:list-item-label>
                           <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                              <fo:block>Relative Delta (not to scale)</fo:block>
                           </fo:list-item-body>
                        </fo:list-item>
                     </fo:list-block>
                  </fo:block>
                  <fo:block id="d274e1121" text-align="center">
                     <fo:external-graphic src="url(file:///home/stbischof/git/OSGI_MIGRATE/osgi_target/org.osgi.service.wireadmin/spec/org.osgi.spec.service.wireadmin/src/main/resources/spec/relative-delta.svg)"
                                          width="auto"
                                          height="auto"
                                          content-width="7.000in"
                                          content-height="1.192in"
                                          text-align="center"/>
                  </fo:block>
               </fo:block>
            </fo:block>
            <fo:block id="d274e1124">
               <fo:block>
                  <fo:block>
                     <fo:block keep-together.within-column="always"
                               margin-left="0pt"
                               font-family="ProductusSemibold,ArialUnicodeMS">
                        <fo:block keep-with-next.within-column="always">
                           <fo:block xmlns:d="http://docbook.org/ns/docbook"
                                     xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink"
                                     font-family="ProductusSemibold,ArialUnicodeMS"
                                     font-weight="normal"
                                     keep-with-next.within-column="always"
                                     space-before.minimum="0.8em"
                                     space-before.optimum="1.0em"
                                     space-before.maximum="1.2em"
                                     text-align="start"
                                     start-indent="0pt"
                                     hyphenate="false">
                              <fo:block font-size="12pt"
                                        line-height="14pt"
                                        space-before="8pt"
                                        space-after="5pt">
                                 <fo:list-block provisional-distance-between-starts="1in"
                                                provisional-label-separation="0.090in">
                                    <fo:list-item>
                                       <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()" text-align="start">
                                          <fo:block>108.7.3</fo:block>
                                       </fo:list-item-label>
                                       <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                                          <fo:block>Hysteresis</fo:block>
                                       </fo:list-item-body>
                                    </fo:list-item>
                                 </fo:list-block>
                              </fo:block>
                           </fo:block>
                        </fo:block>
                     </fo:block>
                  </fo:block>
               </fo:block>
               <fo:block space-before.optimum="5pt"
                         space-before.minimum="5pt"
                         space-before.maximum="5pt">A thermostat is a control device that usually has a hysteresis,
      which means that a heater should be switched on below a certain
      specified low temperature and should be switched off at a specified high
      temperature, where <fo:inline font-style="italic">high</fo:inline> &gt;
      <fo:inline font-style="italic">low</fo:inline>. This is graphically depicted in <fo:basic-link xmlns:d="http://docbook.org/ns/docbook"
                                 xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink"
                                 internal-destination="i1266957">
                     <fo:inline color="inherit"
                                font-family="inherit"
                                letter-spacing="inherit"
                                hyphenate="inherit">Figure 108.9 on page <fo:page-number-citation ref-id="i1266957"/>
                     </fo:inline>
                  </fo:basic-link>. The
      specified acceptable temperatures reduce the amount of start/stops of
      the heater.</fo:block>
               <fo:block space-before.minimum="0.5em"
                         space-before.optimum="1em"
                         space-before.maximum="2em"
                         space-after.minimum="0.5em"
                         space-after.optimum="1em"
                         space-after.maximum="2em"
                         keep-together.within-column="always"
                         id="i1266957">
                  <fo:block xmlns:d="http://docbook.org/ns/docbook"
                            xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink"
                            space-before.optimum="5pt"
                            space-before.minimum="5pt"
                            space-before.maximum="5pt"
                            font-weight="normal"
                            font-size="9pt"
                            hyphenate="false"
                            space-after.minimum="0.4em"
                            space-after.optimum="0.6em"
                            space-after.maximum="0.8em"
                            start-indent="0pt"
                            font-family="Proforma-Book,ArialUnicodeMS"
                            font-style="italic"
                            keep-with-next.within-column="always">
                     <fo:list-block provisional-distance-between-starts="1in"
                                    provisional-label-separation="0.090in">
                        <fo:list-item>
                           <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()" text-align="start">
                              <fo:block>Figure 108.9</fo:block>
                           </fo:list-item-label>
                           <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                              <fo:block>Hysteresis</fo:block>
                           </fo:list-item-body>
                        </fo:list-item>
                     </fo:list-block>
                  </fo:block>
                  <fo:block id="d274e1136" text-align="center">
                     <fo:external-graphic src="url(file:///home/stbischof/git/OSGI_MIGRATE/osgi_target/org.osgi.service.wireadmin/spec/org.osgi.spec.service.wireadmin/src/main/resources/spec/hysteresis.svg)"
                                          width="auto"
                                          height="auto"
                                          content-width="7.000in"
                                          content-height="1.500in"
                                          text-align="center"/>
                  </fo:block>
               </fo:block>
               <fo:block space-before.optimum="5pt"
                         space-before.minimum="5pt"
                         space-before.maximum="5pt">A <fo:inline font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                             font-size="9pt"
                             letter-spacing="0.08em">Consumer</fo:inline> service that controls the heater is only
      interested in events at the top and bottom of the hysteresis. If the
      specified high value is 250 °K and the specified low value is 249 °K,
      the following filter illustrates this concept:</fo:block>
               <fo:block space-before.minimum="0.8em"
                         space-before.optimum="1em"
                         space-before.maximum="1.2em"
                         space-after.minimum="0.8em"
                         space-after.optimum="1em"
                         space-after.maximum="1.2em"
                         hyphenate="false"
                         wrap-option="no-wrap"
                         white-space-collapse="false"
                         white-space-treatment="preserve"
                         linefeed-treatment="preserve"
                         text-align="start"
                         font-family="ProductusOSGiMonoc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                         font-size="9pt"
                         letter-spacing="-.0em"
                         space-before="5pt"
                         space-after="3pt"
                         space-after.conditionality="retain"
                         start-indent="inherit"
                         line-height="11pt"
                         id="d274e1143">(|(&amp;(wirevalue.previous&lt;=250)(wirevalue.current&gt;250))
    (&amp;(wirevalue.previous&gt;=249)(wirevalue.current&lt;249))
)</fo:block>
            </fo:block>
         </fo:block>
         <fo:block id="i1303529">
            <fo:block>
               <fo:block>
                  <fo:block keep-together.within-column="always"
                            margin-left="0pt"
                            font-family="ProductusSemibold,ArialUnicodeMS">
                     <fo:block keep-with-next.within-column="always">
                        <fo:block xmlns:d="http://docbook.org/ns/docbook"
                                  xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink"
                                  font-family="ProductusSemibold,ArialUnicodeMS"
                                  font-weight="normal"
                                  keep-with-next.within-column="always"
                                  space-before.minimum="0.8em"
                                  space-before.optimum="1.0em"
                                  space-before.maximum="1.2em"
                                  text-align="start"
                                  start-indent="0pt"
                                  hyphenate="false">
                           <fo:marker marker-class-name="section.head.marker">Flavors</fo:marker>
                           <fo:block font-size="18pt"
                                     line-height="25pt"
                                     space-before="12.5pt"
                                     space-after="12pt">
                              <fo:list-block provisional-distance-between-starts="1in"
                                             provisional-label-separation="0.090in">
                                 <fo:list-item>
                                    <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()" text-align="start">
                                       <fo:block>108.8</fo:block>
                                    </fo:list-item-label>
                                    <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                                       <fo:block>Flavors</fo:block>
                                    </fo:list-item-body>
                                 </fo:list-item>
                              </fo:list-block>
                           </fo:block>
                        </fo:block>
                     </fo:block>
                  </fo:block>
               </fo:block>
            </fo:block>
            <fo:block space-before.optimum="5pt"
                      space-before.minimum="5pt"
                      space-before.maximum="5pt">Both <fo:inline font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                          font-size="9pt"
                          letter-spacing="0.08em">Consumer</fo:inline> and <fo:inline font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                          font-size="9pt"
                          letter-spacing="0.08em">Producer</fo:inline> services should
    register with a property describing the classes of the data types they can
    consume or produce respectively. The classes are the
    <fo:inline font-style="italic">flavors</fo:inline> that the service supports. The purpose of
    flavors is to allow an administrative user interface bundle to connect
    Consumer and Producer services. Bundles should only create a connection
    when there is at least one class shared between the flavors from a
    Consumer service and a Producer service. Producer services are responsible
    for selecting the preferred object type from the list of the object types
    preferred by the Consumer service. If the Producer service cannot convert
    its data to any of the flavors listed by the Consumer service,
    <fo:inline font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                          font-size="9pt"
                          letter-spacing="0.08em">null</fo:inline> should be used instead.</fo:block>
         </fo:block>
         <fo:block id="d274e1156">
            <fo:block>
               <fo:block>
                  <fo:block keep-together.within-column="always"
                            margin-left="0pt"
                            font-family="ProductusSemibold,ArialUnicodeMS">
                     <fo:block keep-with-next.within-column="always">
                        <fo:block xmlns:d="http://docbook.org/ns/docbook"
                                  xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink"
                                  font-family="ProductusSemibold,ArialUnicodeMS"
                                  font-weight="normal"
                                  keep-with-next.within-column="always"
                                  space-before.minimum="0.8em"
                                  space-before.optimum="1.0em"
                                  space-before.maximum="1.2em"
                                  text-align="start"
                                  start-indent="0pt"
                                  hyphenate="false">
                           <fo:marker marker-class-name="section.head.marker">Converters</fo:marker>
                           <fo:block font-size="18pt"
                                     line-height="25pt"
                                     space-before="12.5pt"
                                     space-after="12pt">
                              <fo:list-block provisional-distance-between-starts="1in"
                                             provisional-label-separation="0.090in">
                                 <fo:list-item>
                                    <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()" text-align="start">
                                       <fo:block>108.9</fo:block>
                                    </fo:list-item-label>
                                    <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                                       <fo:block>Converters</fo:block>
                                    </fo:list-item-body>
                                 </fo:list-item>
                              </fo:list-block>
                           </fo:block>
                        </fo:block>
                     </fo:block>
                  </fo:block>
               </fo:block>
            </fo:block>
            <fo:block space-before.optimum="5pt"
                      space-before.minimum="5pt"
                      space-before.maximum="5pt">A converter is a bundle that registers a Consumer and a Producer
    service that are related and performs data conversions. Data values
    delivered to the Consumer service are processed and transferred via the
    related Producer service. The Producer service sends the converted data to
    other Consumer services. This is shown in <fo:basic-link xmlns:d="http://docbook.org/ns/docbook"
                              xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink"
                              internal-destination="i1287154">
                  <fo:inline color="inherit"
                             font-family="inherit"
                             letter-spacing="inherit"
                             hyphenate="inherit">Figure 108.10</fo:inline>
               </fo:basic-link>.</fo:block>
            <fo:block space-before.minimum="0.5em"
                      space-before.optimum="1em"
                      space-before.maximum="2em"
                      space-after.minimum="0.5em"
                      space-after.optimum="1em"
                      space-after.maximum="2em"
                      keep-together.within-column="always"
                      id="i1287154">
               <fo:block xmlns:d="http://docbook.org/ns/docbook"
                         xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink"
                         space-before.optimum="5pt"
                         space-before.minimum="5pt"
                         space-before.maximum="5pt"
                         font-weight="normal"
                         font-size="9pt"
                         hyphenate="false"
                         space-after.minimum="0.4em"
                         space-after.optimum="0.6em"
                         space-after.maximum="0.8em"
                         start-indent="0pt"
                         font-family="Proforma-Book,ArialUnicodeMS"
                         font-style="italic"
                         keep-with-next.within-column="always">
                  <fo:list-block provisional-distance-between-starts="1in"
                                 provisional-label-separation="0.090in">
                     <fo:list-item>
                        <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()" text-align="start">
                           <fo:block>Figure 108.10</fo:block>
                        </fo:list-item-label>
                        <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                           <fo:block>Converter (for legend see <fo:basic-link internal-destination="i1276764">
                                 <fo:inline color="inherit"
                                            font-family="inherit"
                                            letter-spacing="inherit"
                                            hyphenate="inherit">Figure 108.2</fo:inline>
                              </fo:basic-link> )</fo:block>
                        </fo:list-item-body>
                     </fo:list-item>
                  </fo:list-block>
               </fo:block>
               <fo:block id="d274e1167" text-align="center">
                  <fo:external-graphic src="url(file:///home/stbischof/git/OSGI_MIGRATE/osgi_target/org.osgi.service.wireadmin/spec/org.osgi.spec.service.wireadmin/src/main/resources/spec/converter.svg)"
                                       width="auto"
                                       height="auto"
                                       content-width="7.000in"
                                       content-height="1.040in"
                                       text-align="center"/>
               </fo:block>
            </fo:block>
         </fo:block>
         <fo:block id="d274e1171">
            <fo:block>
               <fo:block>
                  <fo:block keep-together.within-column="always"
                            margin-left="0pt"
                            font-family="ProductusSemibold,ArialUnicodeMS">
                     <fo:block keep-with-next.within-column="always">
                        <fo:block xmlns:d="http://docbook.org/ns/docbook"
                                  xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink"
                                  font-family="ProductusSemibold,ArialUnicodeMS"
                                  font-weight="normal"
                                  keep-with-next.within-column="always"
                                  space-before.minimum="0.8em"
                                  space-before.optimum="1.0em"
                                  space-before.maximum="1.2em"
                                  text-align="start"
                                  start-indent="0pt"
                                  hyphenate="false">
                           <fo:marker marker-class-name="section.head.marker">Wire Admin Service Implementation</fo:marker>
                           <fo:block font-size="18pt"
                                     line-height="25pt"
                                     space-before="12.5pt"
                                     space-after="12pt">
                              <fo:list-block provisional-distance-between-starts="1in"
                                             provisional-label-separation="0.090in">
                                 <fo:list-item>
                                    <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()" text-align="start">
                                       <fo:block>108.10</fo:block>
                                    </fo:list-item-label>
                                    <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                                       <fo:block>Wire Admin Service Implementation</fo:block>
                                    </fo:list-item-body>
                                 </fo:list-item>
                              </fo:list-block>
                           </fo:block>
                        </fo:block>
                     </fo:block>
                  </fo:block>
               </fo:block>
            </fo:block>
            <fo:block space-before.optimum="5pt"
                      space-before.minimum="5pt"
                      space-before.maximum="5pt">The Wire Admin service is the administrative service that is used to
    control the wiring topology in the OSGi Framework. It contains methods to
    create or update wires, delete wires, and list existing wires. It is
    intended to be used by user interfaces or management programs that control
    the wiring topology of the OSGi Framework.</fo:block>
            <fo:block space-before.optimum="5pt"
                      space-before.minimum="5pt"
                      space-before.maximum="5pt">The <fo:basic-link xmlns:d="http://docbook.org/ns/docbook"
                              xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink"
                              internal-destination="org.osgi.service.wireadmin.WireAdmin.createWire-String-String-Dictionary-">
                  <fo:inline color="blue"
                             font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                             letter-spacing="0.08em"
                             hyphenate="false">createWire(String,String,Dictionary)</fo:inline>
               </fo:basic-link> method is used to associate a Producer service
    with a Consumer service. The method always creates and returns a new
    object. It is therefore possible to create multiple, distinct wires
    between a Producer and a Consumer service. The properties can be used to
    create multiple associations between Producer and Consumer services in
    that act in different ways.</fo:block>
            <fo:block space-before.optimum="5pt"
                      space-before.minimum="5pt"
                      space-before.maximum="5pt">The properties of a <fo:inline font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                          font-size="9pt"
                          letter-spacing="0.08em">Wire</fo:inline> object can be updated with the
    <fo:basic-link xmlns:d="http://docbook.org/ns/docbook"
                              xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink"
                              internal-destination="org.osgi.service.wireadmin.Wire.update-Object-">
                  <fo:inline color="blue"
                             font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                             letter-spacing="0.08em"
                             hyphenate="false">update(Object)</fo:inline>
               </fo:basic-link> method. This method must update the properties in
    the Wire object and must notify the associated Consumer and Producer
    services if they are registered. <fo:inline font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                          font-size="9pt"
                          letter-spacing="0.08em">Wire</fo:inline> objects that are no
    longer needed can be removed with the <fo:basic-link xmlns:d="http://docbook.org/ns/docbook"
                              xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink"
                              internal-destination="org.osgi.service.wireadmin.WireAdmin.deleteWire-Wire-">
                  <fo:inline color="blue"
                             font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                             letter-spacing="0.08em"
                             hyphenate="false">deleteWire(Wire)</fo:inline>
               </fo:basic-link> method. All these methods are in the
    <fo:inline font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                          font-size="9pt"
                          letter-spacing="0.08em">WireAdmin</fo:inline> class and not in the <fo:inline font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                          font-size="9pt"
                          letter-spacing="0.08em">Wire</fo:inline> class for
    security reasons. See <fo:basic-link xmlns:d="http://docbook.org/ns/docbook"
                              xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink"
                              internal-destination="i1287360">
                  <fo:inline color="inherit"
                             font-family="inherit"
                             letter-spacing="inherit"
                             hyphenate="inherit">
                     <fo:inline font-style="italic">Security</fo:inline> on page <fo:page-number-citation ref-id="i1287360"/>
                  </fo:inline>
               </fo:basic-link>.</fo:block>
            <fo:block space-before.optimum="5pt"
                      space-before.minimum="5pt"
                      space-before.maximum="5pt">The <fo:basic-link xmlns:d="http://docbook.org/ns/docbook"
                              xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink"
                              internal-destination="org.osgi.service.wireadmin.WireAdmin.getWires-String-">
                  <fo:inline color="blue"
                             font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                             letter-spacing="0.08em"
                             hyphenate="false">getWires(String)</fo:inline>
               </fo:basic-link> method returns an array of <fo:inline font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                          font-size="9pt"
                          letter-spacing="0.08em">Wire</fo:inline>
    objects (or <fo:inline font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                          font-size="9pt"
                          letter-spacing="0.08em">null</fo:inline>). All objects are returned when the filter
    argument is <fo:inline font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                          font-size="9pt"
                          letter-spacing="0.08em">null</fo:inline>. Specifying a filter argument limits the
    returned objects. The filter uses the same syntax as the Framework Filter
    specification. This filter is applied to the properties of the
    <fo:inline font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                          font-size="9pt"
                          letter-spacing="0.08em">Wire</fo:inline> object and only <fo:inline font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                          font-size="9pt"
                          letter-spacing="0.08em">Wire</fo:inline> objects that match
    this filter are returned.</fo:block>
            <fo:block space-before.optimum="5pt"
                      space-before.minimum="5pt"
                      space-before.maximum="5pt">The following example shows how the <fo:inline font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                          font-size="9pt"
                          letter-spacing="0.08em">getWires</fo:inline> method can
    be used to print the PIDs of <fo:inline font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                          font-size="9pt"
                          letter-spacing="0.08em">Producer</fo:inline> services that are wired
    to a specific <fo:inline font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                          font-size="9pt"
                          letter-spacing="0.08em">Consumer</fo:inline> service.</fo:block>
            <fo:block space-before.minimum="0.8em"
                      space-before.optimum="1em"
                      space-before.maximum="1.2em"
                      space-after.minimum="0.8em"
                      space-after.optimum="1em"
                      space-after.maximum="1.2em"
                      hyphenate="false"
                      wrap-option="no-wrap"
                      white-space-collapse="false"
                      white-space-treatment="preserve"
                      linefeed-treatment="preserve"
                      text-align="start"
                      font-family="ProductusOSGiMonoc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                      font-size="9pt"
                      letter-spacing="-.0em"
                      space-before="5pt"
                      space-after="3pt"
                      space-after.conditionality="retain"
                      start-indent="inherit"
                      line-height="11pt"
                      id="d274e1218">String f = "(wireadmin.consumer.pid=com.acme.x)";
Wire [] wires = getWireAdmin().getWires( f );
for ( int i=0; wires != null &amp;&amp; i &lt; wires.length;i++ )
    System.out.println( 
        wires[i].getProperties().get( 
            "wireadmin.producer.pid") 
    );</fo:block>
         </fo:block>
         <fo:block id="i1622432">
            <fo:block>
               <fo:block>
                  <fo:block keep-together.within-column="always"
                            margin-left="0pt"
                            font-family="ProductusSemibold,ArialUnicodeMS">
                     <fo:block keep-with-next.within-column="always">
                        <fo:block xmlns:d="http://docbook.org/ns/docbook"
                                  xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink"
                                  font-family="ProductusSemibold,ArialUnicodeMS"
                                  font-weight="normal"
                                  keep-with-next.within-column="always"
                                  space-before.minimum="0.8em"
                                  space-before.optimum="1.0em"
                                  space-before.maximum="1.2em"
                                  text-align="start"
                                  start-indent="0pt"
                                  hyphenate="false">
                           <fo:marker marker-class-name="section.head.marker">Wire Admin Listener Service Events</fo:marker>
                           <fo:block font-size="18pt"
                                     line-height="25pt"
                                     space-before="12.5pt"
                                     space-after="12pt">
                              <fo:list-block provisional-distance-between-starts="1in"
                                             provisional-label-separation="0.090in">
                                 <fo:list-item>
                                    <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()" text-align="start">
                                       <fo:block>108.11</fo:block>
                                    </fo:list-item-label>
                                    <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                                       <fo:block>Wire Admin Listener Service Events</fo:block>
                                    </fo:list-item-body>
                                 </fo:list-item>
                              </fo:list-block>
                           </fo:block>
                        </fo:block>
                     </fo:block>
                  </fo:block>
               </fo:block>
            </fo:block>
            <fo:block space-before.optimum="5pt"
                      space-before.minimum="5pt"
                      space-before.maximum="5pt">The Wire Admin service has an extensive list of events that it can
    deliver. The events allow other bundles to track changes in the topology
    as they happen. For example, a graphic user interface program can use the
    events to show when <fo:inline font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                          font-size="9pt"
                          letter-spacing="0.08em">Wire</fo:inline> objects become connected, when these
    objects are deleted, and when data flows over a Wire object.</fo:block>
            <fo:block space-before.optimum="5pt"
                      space-before.minimum="5pt"
                      space-before.maximum="5pt">A bundle that is interested in such events must register a
    <fo:inline font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                          font-size="9pt"
                          letter-spacing="0.08em">WireAdminListener</fo:inline> service object with a special
    <fo:inline font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                          font-size="9pt"
                          letter-spacing="0.08em">Integer</fo:inline> property <fo:inline font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                          font-size="9pt"
                          letter-spacing="0.08em">WIREADMIN_EVENTS</fo:inline> ("
    <fo:inline font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                          font-size="9pt"
                          letter-spacing="0.08em">wireadmin.events</fo:inline>"). This <fo:inline font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                          font-size="9pt"
                          letter-spacing="0.08em">Integer</fo:inline> object contains
    a bitmap of all the events in which this Wire Admin Listener service is
    interested (events have associated constants that can be ORed together). A
    Wire Admin service must not deliver events to the Wire Admin Listener
    service when that event type is not in the bitmap. If no such property is
    registered, no events are delivered to the Wire Admin Listener
    service.</fo:block>
            <fo:block space-before.optimum="5pt"
                      space-before.minimum="5pt"
                      space-before.maximum="5pt">The <fo:inline font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                          font-size="9pt"
                          letter-spacing="0.08em">WireAdminListener</fo:inline> interface has only one method:
    <fo:basic-link xmlns:d="http://docbook.org/ns/docbook"
                              xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink"
                              internal-destination="org.osgi.service.wireadmin.WireAdminListener.wireAdminEvent-WireAdminEvent-">
                  <fo:inline color="blue"
                             font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                             letter-spacing="0.08em"
                             hyphenate="false">wireAdminEvent(WireAdminEvent)</fo:inline>
               </fo:basic-link>. The argument is a <fo:inline font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                          font-size="9pt"
                          letter-spacing="0.08em">WireAdminEvent</fo:inline>
    object that contains the event type and associated data.</fo:block>
            <fo:block space-before.optimum="5pt"
                      space-before.minimum="5pt"
                      space-before.maximum="5pt">A <fo:inline font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                          font-size="9pt"
                          letter-spacing="0.08em">WireAdminEvent</fo:inline> object can be sent asynchronously but
    must be ordered for each Wire Admin Listener service. The way events must
    be delivered is the same as described in <fo:inline font-style="italic">Delivering
    Events</fo:inline> of <fo:inline color="inherit"
                          font-family="inherit"
                          letter-spacing="inherit"
                          hyphenate="inherit">???</fo:inline>. Wire Admin Listener services must not assume
    that the state reflected by the event is still true when they receive the
    event.</fo:block>
            <fo:block space-before.optimum="5pt"
                      space-before.minimum="5pt"
                      space-before.maximum="5pt">The following types are defined for a <fo:inline font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                          font-size="9pt"
                          letter-spacing="0.08em">WireEvent</fo:inline>
    object:</fo:block>
            <fo:block xmlns:rx="http://www.renderx.com/XSL/Extensions"
                      space-before.minimum="0.5em"
                      space-before.optimum="1em"
                      space-before.maximum="2em"
                      space-after.minimum="0.5em"
                      space-after.optimum="1em"
                      space-after.maximum="2em"
                      keep-together.within-column="auto"
                      id="d274e1257">
               <fo:block xmlns:d="http://docbook.org/ns/docbook"
                         xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink"
                         space-before.optimum="5pt"
                         space-before.minimum="5pt"
                         space-before.maximum="5pt"
                         font-weight="normal"
                         font-size="9pt"
                         hyphenate="false"
                         space-after.minimum="0.4em"
                         space-after.optimum="0.6em"
                         space-after.maximum="0.8em"
                         start-indent="0pt"
                         font-family="Proforma-Book,ArialUnicodeMS"
                         font-style="italic"
                         keep-with-next.within-column="always">
                  <fo:list-block provisional-distance-between-starts="1in"
                                 provisional-label-separation="0.090in">
                     <fo:list-item>
                        <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()" text-align="start">
                           <fo:block>Table 108.4</fo:block>
                        </fo:list-item-label>
                        <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                           <fo:block>Events</fo:block>
                        </fo:list-item-body>
                     </fo:list-item>
                  </fo:list-block>
               </fo:block>
               <fo:table border-before-width.conditionality="retain"
                         border-collapse="collapse"
                         table-layout="fixed"
                         width="100%">
                  <fo:table-column column-number="1" column-width="proportional-column-width(2)"/>
                  <fo:table-column column-number="2" column-width="proportional-column-width(3)"/>
                  <fo:table-header start-indent="0pt" end-indent="0pt">
                     <fo:table-row keep-together.within-column="always"
                                   keep-with-next.within-column="always"
                                   font-family="ProductusSemibold,ArialUnicodeMS">
                        <fo:table-cell padding-start="0pt"
                                       padding-end="4pt"
                                       padding-top="1pt"
                                       padding-bottom="1pt">
                           <fo:block>Event type</fo:block>
                        </fo:table-cell>
                        <fo:table-cell padding-start="0pt"
                                       padding-end="4pt"
                                       padding-top="1pt"
                                       padding-bottom="1pt">
                           <fo:block>Description</fo:block>
                        </fo:table-cell>
                     </fo:table-row>
                  </fo:table-header>
                  <fo:table-body start-indent="0pt" end-indent="0pt">
                     <fo:table-row keep-together.within-column="always">
                        <fo:table-cell padding-start="0pt"
                                       padding-end="4pt"
                                       padding-top="1pt"
                                       padding-bottom="1pt">
                           <fo:block>
                              <fo:inline font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                                         font-size="9pt"
                                         letter-spacing="0.08em">WIRE_CREATED</fo:inline>
                           </fo:block>
                        </fo:table-cell>
                        <fo:table-cell padding-start="0pt"
                                       padding-end="4pt"
                                       padding-top="1pt"
                                       padding-bottom="1pt">
                           <fo:block>
                              <fo:block space-before.optimum="5pt"
                                        space-before.minimum="5pt"
                                        space-before.maximum="5pt">A new <fo:inline font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                                            font-size="9pt"
                                            letter-spacing="0.08em">Wire</fo:inline> object has been
            created.</fo:block>
                           </fo:block>
                        </fo:table-cell>
                     </fo:table-row>
                     <fo:table-row keep-together.within-column="always">
                        <fo:table-cell padding-start="0pt"
                                       padding-end="4pt"
                                       padding-top="1pt"
                                       padding-bottom="1pt">
                           <fo:block>
                              <fo:inline font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                                         font-size="9pt"
                                         letter-spacing="0.08em">WIRE_CONNECTED</fo:inline>
                           </fo:block>
                        </fo:table-cell>
                        <fo:table-cell padding-start="0pt"
                                       padding-end="4pt"
                                       padding-top="1pt"
                                       padding-bottom="1pt">
                           <fo:block>
                              <fo:block space-before.optimum="5pt"
                                        space-before.minimum="5pt"
                                        space-before.maximum="5pt">Both the <fo:inline font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                                            font-size="9pt"
                                            letter-spacing="0.08em">Producer</fo:inline> service and the
            <fo:inline font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                                            font-size="9pt"
                                            letter-spacing="0.08em">Consumer</fo:inline> service are registered but may not have
            executed their respective
            <fo:inline font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                                            font-size="9pt"
                                            letter-spacing="0.08em">connectedProducers/connectedConsumers</fo:inline>
            methods.</fo:block>
                           </fo:block>
                        </fo:table-cell>
                     </fo:table-row>
                     <fo:table-row keep-together.within-column="always">
                        <fo:table-cell padding-start="0pt"
                                       padding-end="4pt"
                                       padding-top="1pt"
                                       padding-bottom="1pt">
                           <fo:block>
                              <fo:inline font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                                         font-size="9pt"
                                         letter-spacing="0.08em">WIRE_UPDATED</fo:inline>
                           </fo:block>
                        </fo:table-cell>
                        <fo:table-cell padding-start="0pt"
                                       padding-end="4pt"
                                       padding-top="1pt"
                                       padding-bottom="1pt">
                           <fo:block>
                              <fo:block space-before.optimum="5pt"
                                        space-before.minimum="5pt"
                                        space-before.maximum="5pt">The <fo:inline font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                                            font-size="9pt"
                                            letter-spacing="0.08em">Wire</fo:inline> object's properties have been
            updated.</fo:block>
                           </fo:block>
                        </fo:table-cell>
                     </fo:table-row>
                     <fo:table-row keep-together.within-column="always">
                        <fo:table-cell padding-start="0pt"
                                       padding-end="4pt"
                                       padding-top="1pt"
                                       padding-bottom="1pt">
                           <fo:block>
                              <fo:inline font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                                         font-size="9pt"
                                         letter-spacing="0.08em">WIRE_TRACE</fo:inline>
                           </fo:block>
                        </fo:table-cell>
                        <fo:table-cell padding-start="0pt"
                                       padding-end="4pt"
                                       padding-top="1pt"
                                       padding-bottom="1pt">
                           <fo:block>
                              <fo:block space-before.optimum="5pt"
                                        space-before.minimum="5pt"
                                        space-before.maximum="5pt">The Consumer has seen a new value, either after the
            Producer service has called the <fo:inline font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                                            font-size="9pt"
                                            letter-spacing="0.08em">Wire</fo:inline>. <fo:basic-link xmlns:d="http://docbook.org/ns/docbook"
                                                xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink"
                                                internal-destination="org.osgi.service.wireadmin.Wire.update-Object-">
                                    <fo:inline color="blue"
                                               font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                                               letter-spacing="0.08em"
                                               hyphenate="false">update(Object)</fo:inline>
                                 </fo:basic-link> method and the value was not filtered, or
            the <fo:inline font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                                            font-size="9pt"
                                            letter-spacing="0.08em">Producer</fo:inline> service has returned from the <fo:basic-link xmlns:d="http://docbook.org/ns/docbook"
                                                xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink"
                                                internal-destination="org.osgi.service.wireadmin.Producer.polled-Wire-">
                                    <fo:inline color="blue"
                                               font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                                               letter-spacing="0.08em"
                                               hyphenate="false">polled(Wire)</fo:inline>
                                 </fo:basic-link> method.</fo:block>
                           </fo:block>
                        </fo:table-cell>
                     </fo:table-row>
                     <fo:table-row keep-together.within-column="always">
                        <fo:table-cell padding-start="0pt"
                                       padding-end="4pt"
                                       padding-top="1pt"
                                       padding-bottom="1pt">
                           <fo:block>
                              <fo:inline font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                                         font-size="9pt"
                                         letter-spacing="0.08em">WIRE_DISCONNECTED</fo:inline>
                           </fo:block>
                        </fo:table-cell>
                        <fo:table-cell padding-start="0pt"
                                       padding-end="4pt"
                                       padding-top="1pt"
                                       padding-bottom="1pt">
                           <fo:block>
                              <fo:block space-before.optimum="5pt"
                                        space-before.minimum="5pt"
                                        space-before.maximum="5pt">The Producer service or Consumer service have become
            unregistered and the <fo:inline font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                                            font-size="9pt"
                                            letter-spacing="0.08em">Wire</fo:inline> object is no longer
            connected.</fo:block>
                           </fo:block>
                        </fo:table-cell>
                     </fo:table-row>
                     <fo:table-row keep-together.within-column="always">
                        <fo:table-cell padding-start="0pt"
                                       padding-end="4pt"
                                       padding-top="1pt"
                                       padding-bottom="1pt">
                           <fo:block>
                              <fo:inline font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                                         font-size="9pt"
                                         letter-spacing="0.08em">WIRE_DELETED</fo:inline>
                           </fo:block>
                        </fo:table-cell>
                        <fo:table-cell padding-start="0pt"
                                       padding-end="4pt"
                                       padding-top="1pt"
                                       padding-bottom="1pt">
                           <fo:block>
                              <fo:block space-before.optimum="5pt"
                                        space-before.minimum="5pt"
                                        space-before.maximum="5pt">The <fo:inline font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                                            font-size="9pt"
                                            letter-spacing="0.08em">Wire</fo:inline> object is deleted from the
            repository and is no longer available from the
            <fo:inline font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                                            font-size="9pt"
                                            letter-spacing="0.08em">getWires</fo:inline> method.</fo:block>
                           </fo:block>
                        </fo:table-cell>
                     </fo:table-row>
                     <fo:table-row keep-together.within-column="always">
                        <fo:table-cell padding-start="0pt"
                                       padding-end="4pt"
                                       padding-top="1pt"
                                       padding-bottom="1pt">
                           <fo:block>
                              <fo:inline font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                                         font-size="9pt"
                                         letter-spacing="0.08em">CONSUMER_EXCEPTION</fo:inline>
                           </fo:block>
                        </fo:table-cell>
                        <fo:table-cell padding-start="0pt"
                                       padding-end="4pt"
                                       padding-top="1pt"
                                       padding-bottom="1pt">
                           <fo:block>
                              <fo:block space-before.optimum="5pt"
                                        space-before.minimum="5pt"
                                        space-before.maximum="5pt">The Consumer service generated an exception and the
            exception is included in the event.</fo:block>
                           </fo:block>
                        </fo:table-cell>
                     </fo:table-row>
                     <fo:table-row keep-together.within-column="always">
                        <fo:table-cell padding-start="0pt"
                                       padding-end="4pt"
                                       padding-top="1pt"
                                       padding-bottom="1pt">
                           <fo:block>
                              <fo:inline font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                                         font-size="9pt"
                                         letter-spacing="0.08em">PRODUCER_EXCEPTION</fo:inline>
                           </fo:block>
                        </fo:table-cell>
                        <fo:table-cell padding-start="0pt"
                                       padding-end="4pt"
                                       padding-top="1pt"
                                       padding-bottom="1pt">
                           <fo:block>
                              <fo:block space-before.optimum="5pt"
                                        space-before.minimum="5pt"
                                        space-before.maximum="5pt">The Producer service generated an exception in a
            callback and the exception is included in the
            event.</fo:block>
                           </fo:block>
                        </fo:table-cell>
                     </fo:table-row>
                  </fo:table-body>
               </fo:table>
            </fo:block>
            <fo:block id="d274e1337">
               <fo:block>
                  <fo:block>
                     <fo:block keep-together.within-column="always"
                               margin-left="0pt"
                               font-family="ProductusSemibold,ArialUnicodeMS">
                        <fo:block keep-with-next.within-column="always">
                           <fo:block xmlns:d="http://docbook.org/ns/docbook"
                                     xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink"
                                     font-family="ProductusSemibold,ArialUnicodeMS"
                                     font-weight="normal"
                                     keep-with-next.within-column="always"
                                     space-before.minimum="0.8em"
                                     space-before.optimum="1.0em"
                                     space-before.maximum="1.2em"
                                     text-align="start"
                                     start-indent="0pt"
                                     hyphenate="false">
                              <fo:block font-size="12pt"
                                        line-height="14pt"
                                        space-before="8pt"
                                        space-after="5pt">
                                 <fo:list-block provisional-distance-between-starts="1in"
                                                provisional-label-separation="0.090in">
                                    <fo:list-item>
                                       <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()" text-align="start">
                                          <fo:block>108.11.1</fo:block>
                                       </fo:list-item-label>
                                       <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                                          <fo:block>Event Admin Service Events</fo:block>
                                       </fo:list-item-body>
                                    </fo:list-item>
                                 </fo:list-block>
                              </fo:block>
                           </fo:block>
                        </fo:block>
                     </fo:block>
                  </fo:block>
               </fo:block>
               <fo:block space-before.optimum="5pt"
                         space-before.minimum="5pt"
                         space-before.maximum="5pt">Wire admin events must be sent asynchronously to the Event Admin
      service by the Wire Admin implementation, if present. The topic of a
      Wire Admin Event is one of the following:</fo:block>
               <fo:block space-before.minimum="0.8em"
                         space-before.optimum="1em"
                         space-before.maximum="1.2em"
                         space-after.minimum="0.8em"
                         space-after.optimum="1em"
                         space-after.maximum="1.2em"
                         hyphenate="false"
                         wrap-option="no-wrap"
                         white-space-collapse="false"
                         white-space-treatment="preserve"
                         linefeed-treatment="preserve"
                         text-align="start"
                         font-family="ProductusOSGiMonoc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                         font-size="9pt"
                         letter-spacing="-.0em"
                         space-before="5pt"
                         space-after="3pt"
                         space-after.conditionality="retain"
                         start-indent="inherit"
                         line-height="11pt"
                         id="d274e1340">org/osgi/service/wireadmin/WireAdminEvent/&lt;eventtype&gt;</fo:block>
               <fo:block space-before.optimum="5pt"
                         space-before.minimum="5pt"
                         space-before.maximum="5pt">The following event types are supported:</fo:block>
               <fo:block space-before.minimum="0.8em"
                         space-before.optimum="1em"
                         space-before.maximum="1.2em"
                         space-after.minimum="0.8em"
                         space-after.optimum="1em"
                         space-after.maximum="1.2em"
                         hyphenate="false"
                         wrap-option="no-wrap"
                         white-space-collapse="false"
                         white-space-treatment="preserve"
                         linefeed-treatment="preserve"
                         text-align="start"
                         font-family="ProductusOSGiMonoc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                         font-size="9pt"
                         letter-spacing="-.0em"
                         space-before="5pt"
                         space-after="3pt"
                         space-after.conditionality="retain"
                         start-indent="inherit"
                         line-height="11pt"
                         id="d274e1342">WIRE_CREATED
WIRE_CONNECTED
WIRE_UPDATED
WIRE_TRACE
WIRE_DISCONNECTED
WIRE_DELETED
PRODUCER_EXCEPTION
CONSUMER_EXCEPTION</fo:block>
               <fo:block space-before.optimum="5pt"
                         space-before.minimum="5pt"
                         space-before.maximum="5pt">The properties of a wire admin event are the following.</fo:block>
               <fo:list-block space-before.optimum="1em"
                              space-before.minimum="0.8em"
                              space-before.maximum="1.2em"
                              space-after.optimum="1em"
                              space-after.minimum="0.8em"
                              space-after.maximum="1.2em"
                              provisional-label-separation="0.2em"
                              provisional-distance-between-starts="12pt"
                              id="d274e1344">
                  <fo:list-item space-before.optimum="2pt"
                                space-before.minimum="2pt"
                                space-before.maximum="2pt"
                                id="d274e1345">
                     <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                        <fo:block>•</fo:block>
                     </fo:list-item-label>
                     <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                        <fo:block>
                           <fo:block>
                              <fo:inline font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                                         font-size="9pt"
                                         letter-spacing="0.08em">event</fo:inline> - (<fo:inline font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                                         font-size="9pt"
                                         letter-spacing="0.08em">WireAdminEvent)</fo:inline> The
          <fo:inline font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                                         font-size="9pt"
                                         letter-spacing="0.08em">WireAdminEvent</fo:inline> object broadcast by the Wire Admin
          service.</fo:block>
                        </fo:block>
                     </fo:list-item-body>
                  </fo:list-item>
               </fo:list-block>
               <fo:block space-before.optimum="5pt"
                         space-before.minimum="5pt"
                         space-before.maximum="5pt">If the <fo:inline font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                             font-size="9pt"
                             letter-spacing="0.08em">getWire</fo:inline> method returns a non <fo:inline font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                             font-size="9pt"
                             letter-spacing="0.08em">null</fo:inline>
      value:</fo:block>
               <fo:list-block space-before.optimum="1em"
                              space-before.minimum="0.8em"
                              space-before.maximum="1.2em"
                              space-after.optimum="1em"
                              space-after.minimum="0.8em"
                              space-after.maximum="1.2em"
                              provisional-label-separation="0.2em"
                              provisional-distance-between-starts="12pt"
                              id="d274e1359">
                  <fo:list-item space-before.optimum="2pt"
                                space-before.minimum="2pt"
                                space-before.maximum="2pt"
                                id="d274e1360">
                     <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                        <fo:block>•</fo:block>
                     </fo:list-item-label>
                     <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                        <fo:block>
                           <fo:block>
                              <fo:inline font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                                         font-size="9pt"
                                         letter-spacing="0.08em">wire</fo:inline> - (<fo:inline font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                                         font-size="9pt"
                                         letter-spacing="0.08em">Wire</fo:inline>) The <fo:inline font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                                         font-size="9pt"
                                         letter-spacing="0.08em">Wire</fo:inline>
          object returned by the <fo:inline font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                                         font-size="9pt"
                                         letter-spacing="0.08em">getWire</fo:inline> method.</fo:block>
                        </fo:block>
                     </fo:list-item-body>
                  </fo:list-item>
                  <fo:list-item space-before.optimum="2pt"
                                space-before.minimum="2pt"
                                space-before.maximum="2pt"
                                id="d274e1370">
                     <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                        <fo:block>•</fo:block>
                     </fo:list-item-label>
                     <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                        <fo:block>
                           <fo:block>
                              <fo:inline font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                                         font-size="9pt"
                                         letter-spacing="0.08em">wire.flavors</fo:inline> - (<fo:inline font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                                         font-size="9pt"
                                         letter-spacing="0.08em">String[])</fo:inline> The names
          of the classes returned by the <fo:inline font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                                         font-size="9pt"
                                         letter-spacing="0.08em">Wire</fo:inline>
                              <fo:inline font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                                         font-size="9pt"
                                         letter-spacing="0.08em">getFlavors</fo:inline> method.</fo:block>
                        </fo:block>
                     </fo:list-item-body>
                  </fo:list-item>
                  <fo:list-item space-before.optimum="2pt"
                                space-before.minimum="2pt"
                                space-before.maximum="2pt"
                                id="d274e1380">
                     <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                        <fo:block>•</fo:block>
                     </fo:list-item-label>
                     <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                        <fo:block>
                           <fo:block>
                              <fo:inline font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                                         font-size="9pt"
                                         letter-spacing="0.08em">wire.scope</fo:inline> - (<fo:inline font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                                         font-size="9pt"
                                         letter-spacing="0.08em">String[])</fo:inline> The scope of
          the <fo:inline font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                                         font-size="9pt"
                                         letter-spacing="0.08em">Wire</fo:inline> object, as returned by its
          <fo:inline font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                                         font-size="9pt"
                                         letter-spacing="0.08em">getScope</fo:inline> method.</fo:block>
                        </fo:block>
                     </fo:list-item-body>
                  </fo:list-item>
                  <fo:list-item space-before.optimum="2pt"
                                space-before.minimum="2pt"
                                space-before.maximum="2pt"
                                id="d274e1390">
                     <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                        <fo:block>•</fo:block>
                     </fo:list-item-label>
                     <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                        <fo:block>
                           <fo:block>
                              <fo:inline font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                                         font-size="9pt"
                                         letter-spacing="0.08em">wire.connected</fo:inline> - (<fo:inline font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                                         font-size="9pt"
                                         letter-spacing="0.08em">Boolean)</fo:inline> The
          result of the <fo:inline font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                                         font-size="9pt"
                                         letter-spacing="0.08em">Wire</fo:inline>
                              <fo:inline font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                                         font-size="9pt"
                                         letter-spacing="0.08em">isConnected</fo:inline>
          method.</fo:block>
                        </fo:block>
                     </fo:list-item-body>
                  </fo:list-item>
                  <fo:list-item space-before.optimum="2pt"
                                space-before.minimum="2pt"
                                space-before.maximum="2pt"
                                id="d274e1400">
                     <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                        <fo:block>•</fo:block>
                     </fo:list-item-label>
                     <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                        <fo:block>
                           <fo:block>
                              <fo:inline font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                                         font-size="9pt"
                                         letter-spacing="0.08em">wire.valid</fo:inline> - (<fo:inline font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                                         font-size="9pt"
                                         letter-spacing="0.08em">Boolean</fo:inline>) The result of
          the <fo:inline font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                                         font-size="9pt"
                                         letter-spacing="0.08em">Wire isValid</fo:inline> method.</fo:block>
                        </fo:block>
                     </fo:list-item-body>
                  </fo:list-item>
               </fo:list-block>
               <fo:block space-before.optimum="5pt"
                         space-before.minimum="5pt"
                         space-before.maximum="5pt">If the <fo:inline font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                             font-size="9pt"
                             letter-spacing="0.08em">getThrowable</fo:inline> method does not return
      <fo:inline font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                             font-size="9pt"
                             letter-spacing="0.08em">null</fo:inline>:</fo:block>
               <fo:list-block space-before.optimum="1em"
                              space-before.minimum="0.8em"
                              space-before.maximum="1.2em"
                              space-after.optimum="1em"
                              space-after.minimum="0.8em"
                              space-after.maximum="1.2em"
                              provisional-label-separation="0.2em"
                              provisional-distance-between-starts="12pt"
                              id="d274e1414">
                  <fo:list-item space-before.optimum="2pt"
                                space-before.minimum="2pt"
                                space-before.maximum="2pt"
                                id="d274e1415">
                     <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                        <fo:block>•</fo:block>
                     </fo:list-item-label>
                     <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                        <fo:block>
                           <fo:block>
                              <fo:inline font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                                         font-size="9pt"
                                         letter-spacing="0.08em">exception</fo:inline> - (<fo:inline font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                                         font-size="9pt"
                                         letter-spacing="0.08em">Throwable)</fo:inline> The
          Exception returned by the <fo:inline font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                                         font-size="9pt"
                                         letter-spacing="0.08em">getThrowable</fo:inline> method.</fo:block>
                        </fo:block>
                     </fo:list-item-body>
                  </fo:list-item>
                  <fo:list-item space-before.optimum="2pt"
                                space-before.minimum="2pt"
                                space-before.maximum="2pt"
                                id="d274e1423">
                     <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                        <fo:block>•</fo:block>
                     </fo:list-item-label>
                     <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                        <fo:block>
                           <fo:block>
                              <fo:inline font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                                         font-size="9pt"
                                         letter-spacing="0.08em">exception.class</fo:inline> - (<fo:inline font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                                         font-size="9pt"
                                         letter-spacing="0.08em">String)</fo:inline> The
          fully-qualified class name of the related Exception.</fo:block>
                        </fo:block>
                     </fo:list-item-body>
                  </fo:list-item>
                  <fo:list-item space-before.optimum="2pt"
                                space-before.minimum="2pt"
                                space-before.maximum="2pt"
                                id="d274e1429">
                     <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                        <fo:block>•</fo:block>
                     </fo:list-item-label>
                     <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                        <fo:block>
                           <fo:block>
                              <fo:inline font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                                         font-size="9pt"
                                         letter-spacing="0.08em">exception.message</fo:inline> - (<fo:inline font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                                         font-size="9pt"
                                         letter-spacing="0.08em">String)</fo:inline> The
          message of the related Exception</fo:block>
                        </fo:block>
                     </fo:list-item-body>
                  </fo:list-item>
                  <fo:list-item space-before.optimum="2pt"
                                space-before.minimum="2pt"
                                space-before.maximum="2pt"
                                id="d274e1435">
                     <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                        <fo:block>•</fo:block>
                     </fo:list-item-label>
                     <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                        <fo:block>
                           <fo:block>
                              <fo:inline font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                                         font-size="9pt"
                                         letter-spacing="0.08em">service</fo:inline> - (<fo:inline font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                                         font-size="9pt"
                                         letter-spacing="0.08em">ServiceReference)</fo:inline> The
          Service Reference of the Wire Admin service.</fo:block>
                        </fo:block>
                     </fo:list-item-body>
                  </fo:list-item>
                  <fo:list-item space-before.optimum="2pt"
                                space-before.minimum="2pt"
                                space-before.maximum="2pt"
                                id="d274e1441">
                     <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                        <fo:block>•</fo:block>
                     </fo:list-item-label>
                     <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                        <fo:block>
                           <fo:block>
                              <fo:inline font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                                         font-size="9pt"
                                         letter-spacing="0.08em">service.id</fo:inline> - (<fo:inline font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                                         font-size="9pt"
                                         letter-spacing="0.08em">Long)</fo:inline> The service id
          of the WireAdmin service.</fo:block>
                        </fo:block>
                     </fo:list-item-body>
                  </fo:list-item>
                  <fo:list-item space-before.optimum="2pt"
                                space-before.minimum="2pt"
                                space-before.maximum="2pt"
                                id="d274e1447">
                     <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                        <fo:block>•</fo:block>
                     </fo:list-item-label>
                     <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                        <fo:block>
                           <fo:block>
                              <fo:inline font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                                         font-size="9pt"
                                         letter-spacing="0.08em">service.objectClass</fo:inline> - (<fo:inline font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                                         font-size="9pt"
                                         letter-spacing="0.08em">String[])</fo:inline> The
          Wire Admin service's object class (which must include
          <fo:inline font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                                         font-size="9pt"
                                         letter-spacing="0.08em">org.osgi.service.wireadmin.WireAdmin</fo:inline>)</fo:block>
                        </fo:block>
                     </fo:list-item-body>
                  </fo:list-item>
                  <fo:list-item space-before.optimum="2pt"
                                space-before.minimum="2pt"
                                space-before.maximum="2pt"
                                id="d274e1455">
                     <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                        <fo:block>•</fo:block>
                     </fo:list-item-label>
                     <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                        <fo:block>
                           <fo:block>
                              <fo:inline font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                                         font-size="9pt"
                                         letter-spacing="0.08em">service.pid</fo:inline> - (<fo:inline font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                                         font-size="9pt"
                                         letter-spacing="0.08em">String)</fo:inline> The Wire
          Admin service's PID.</fo:block>
                        </fo:block>
                     </fo:list-item-body>
                  </fo:list-item>
               </fo:list-block>
            </fo:block>
         </fo:block>
         <fo:block id="d274e1461">
            <fo:block>
               <fo:block>
                  <fo:block keep-together.within-column="always"
                            margin-left="0pt"
                            font-family="ProductusSemibold,ArialUnicodeMS">
                     <fo:block keep-with-next.within-column="always">
                        <fo:block xmlns:d="http://docbook.org/ns/docbook"
                                  xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink"
                                  font-family="ProductusSemibold,ArialUnicodeMS"
                                  font-weight="normal"
                                  keep-with-next.within-column="always"
                                  space-before.minimum="0.8em"
                                  space-before.optimum="1.0em"
                                  space-before.maximum="1.2em"
                                  text-align="start"
                                  start-indent="0pt"
                                  hyphenate="false">
                           <fo:marker marker-class-name="section.head.marker">Connecting External Entities</fo:marker>
                           <fo:block font-size="18pt"
                                     line-height="25pt"
                                     space-before="12.5pt"
                                     space-after="12pt">
                              <fo:list-block provisional-distance-between-starts="1in"
                                             provisional-label-separation="0.090in">
                                 <fo:list-item>
                                    <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()" text-align="start">
                                       <fo:block>108.12</fo:block>
                                    </fo:list-item-label>
                                    <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                                       <fo:block>Connecting External Entities</fo:block>
                                    </fo:list-item-body>
                                 </fo:list-item>
                              </fo:list-block>
                           </fo:block>
                        </fo:block>
                     </fo:block>
                  </fo:block>
               </fo:block>
            </fo:block>
            <fo:block space-before.optimum="5pt"
                      space-before.minimum="5pt"
                      space-before.maximum="5pt">The Wire Admin service can be used to control the topology of
    consumers and producers that are services, as well as external entities.
    For example, a video camera controlled over an IEEE 1394B bus can be
    registered as a Producer service in the Framework's service registry and a
    TV, also connected to this bus, can be registered as a Consumer service.
    It would be very inefficient to stream the video data through the OSGi
    environment. Therefore, the Wire Admin service can be used to supply the
    external addressing information to the camera and the monitor to make a
    direct connection <fo:inline font-style="italic">outside</fo:inline> the OSGi environment. The
    Wire Admin service provides a uniform mechanism to connect both external
    entities and internal entities.</fo:block>
            <fo:block space-before.minimum="0.5em"
                      space-before.optimum="1em"
                      space-before.maximum="2em"
                      space-after.minimum="0.5em"
                      space-after.optimum="1em"
                      space-after.maximum="2em"
                      keep-together.within-column="always"
                      id="d274e1467">
               <fo:block xmlns:d="http://docbook.org/ns/docbook"
                         xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink"
                         space-before.optimum="5pt"
                         space-before.minimum="5pt"
                         space-before.maximum="5pt"
                         font-weight="normal"
                         font-size="9pt"
                         hyphenate="false"
                         space-after.minimum="0.4em"
                         space-after.optimum="0.6em"
                         space-after.maximum="0.8em"
                         start-indent="0pt"
                         font-family="Proforma-Book,ArialUnicodeMS"
                         font-style="italic"
                         keep-with-next.within-column="always">
                  <fo:list-block provisional-distance-between-starts="1in"
                                 provisional-label-separation="0.090in">
                     <fo:list-item>
                        <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()" text-align="start">
                           <fo:block>Figure 108.11</fo:block>
                        </fo:list-item-label>
                        <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                           <fo:block>Connecting External Entities</fo:block>
                        </fo:list-item-body>
                     </fo:list-item>
                  </fo:list-block>
               </fo:block>
               <fo:block id="d274e1469" text-align="center">
                  <fo:external-graphic src="url(file:///home/stbischof/git/OSGI_MIGRATE/osgi_target/org.osgi.service.wireadmin/spec/org.osgi.spec.service.wireadmin/src/main/resources/spec/connecting-external-entities.svg)"
                                       width="auto"
                                       height="auto"
                                       content-width="7.000in"
                                       content-height="2.279in"
                                       text-align="center"/>
               </fo:block>
            </fo:block>
            <fo:block space-before.optimum="5pt"
                      space-before.minimum="5pt"
                      space-before.maximum="5pt">A Consumer service and a Producer service associated with a
    <fo:inline font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                          font-size="9pt"
                          letter-spacing="0.08em">Wire</fo:inline> object receive enough information to establish a direct
    link because the PIDs of both services are in the <fo:inline font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                          font-size="9pt"
                          letter-spacing="0.08em">Wire</fo:inline>
    object's properties. This situation, however, does not guarantee
    <fo:inline font-style="italic">compatibility</fo:inline> between Producer and the Consumer
    service. It is therefore recommended that flavors are used to ensure this
    compatibility. Producer services that participate in an external
    addressing scheme, like IEEE 1394B, should have a flavor that reflects
    this address. In this case, there should then for example be a IEEE 1394B
    address class. Consumer services that participate in this external
    addressing scheme should only accept data of this flavor.</fo:block>
            <fo:block space-before.optimum="5pt"
                      space-before.minimum="5pt"
                      space-before.maximum="5pt">The OSGi <fo:inline color="inherit"
                          font-family="inherit"
                          letter-spacing="inherit"
                          hyphenate="inherit">???</fo:inline>, defines the concept of a
    device category. This is a description of what classes and properties are
    used in a specific device category: for example, a UPnP device category
    that defines the interface that must be used to register for a UPnP
    device, among other things.</fo:block>
            <fo:block space-before.optimum="5pt"
                      space-before.minimum="5pt"
                      space-before.maximum="5pt">Device category descriptions should include a section that addresses
    the external wiring issue. This section should include what objects are
    send over the wire to exchange addressing information.</fo:block>
         </fo:block>
         <fo:block id="d274e1485">
            <fo:block>
               <fo:block>
                  <fo:block keep-together.within-column="always"
                            margin-left="0pt"
                            font-family="ProductusSemibold,ArialUnicodeMS">
                     <fo:block keep-with-next.within-column="always">
                        <fo:block xmlns:d="http://docbook.org/ns/docbook"
                                  xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink"
                                  font-family="ProductusSemibold,ArialUnicodeMS"
                                  font-weight="normal"
                                  keep-with-next.within-column="always"
                                  space-before.minimum="0.8em"
                                  space-before.optimum="1.0em"
                                  space-before.maximum="1.2em"
                                  text-align="start"
                                  start-indent="0pt"
                                  hyphenate="false">
                           <fo:marker marker-class-name="section.head.marker">Related Standards</fo:marker>
                           <fo:block font-size="18pt"
                                     line-height="25pt"
                                     space-before="12.5pt"
                                     space-after="12pt">
                              <fo:list-block provisional-distance-between-starts="1in"
                                             provisional-label-separation="0.090in">
                                 <fo:list-item>
                                    <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()" text-align="start">
                                       <fo:block>108.13</fo:block>
                                    </fo:list-item-label>
                                    <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                                       <fo:block>Related Standards</fo:block>
                                    </fo:list-item-body>
                                 </fo:list-item>
                              </fo:list-block>
                           </fo:block>
                        </fo:block>
                     </fo:block>
                  </fo:block>
               </fo:block>
            </fo:block>
            <fo:block id="d274e1487">
               <fo:block>
                  <fo:block>
                     <fo:block keep-together.within-column="always"
                               margin-left="0pt"
                               font-family="ProductusSemibold,ArialUnicodeMS">
                        <fo:block keep-with-next.within-column="always">
                           <fo:block xmlns:d="http://docbook.org/ns/docbook"
                                     xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink"
                                     font-family="ProductusSemibold,ArialUnicodeMS"
                                     font-weight="normal"
                                     keep-with-next.within-column="always"
                                     space-before.minimum="0.8em"
                                     space-before.optimum="1.0em"
                                     space-before.maximum="1.2em"
                                     text-align="start"
                                     start-indent="0pt"
                                     hyphenate="false">
                              <fo:block font-size="12pt"
                                        line-height="14pt"
                                        space-before="8pt"
                                        space-after="5pt">
                                 <fo:list-block provisional-distance-between-starts="1in"
                                                provisional-label-separation="0.090in">
                                    <fo:list-item>
                                       <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()" text-align="start">
                                          <fo:block>108.13.1</fo:block>
                                       </fo:list-item-label>
                                       <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                                          <fo:block>Java Beans</fo:block>
                                       </fo:list-item-body>
                                    </fo:list-item>
                                 </fo:list-block>
                              </fo:block>
                           </fo:block>
                        </fo:block>
                     </fo:block>
                  </fo:block>
               </fo:block>
               <fo:block space-before.optimum="5pt"
                         space-before.minimum="5pt"
                         space-before.maximum="5pt">The Wire Admin service leverages the component architecture that
      the Framework service registry offers. Java Beans attempt to achieve
      similar goals. Java Beans are classes that follow a number of
      recommendations that allow them to be configured at run time. The
      techniques that are used by Java Beans during configuration are
      serialization and the construction of adapter classes.</fo:block>
               <fo:block space-before.optimum="5pt"
                         space-before.minimum="5pt"
                         space-before.maximum="5pt">Creating adapter classes in a resource constrained OSGi Framework
      was considered too heavy weight. Also, the dynamic nature of the OSGi
      environment, where services are registered and unregistered
      continuously, creates a mismatch between the intended target area of
      Java Beans and the OSGi Framework.</fo:block>
               <fo:block space-before.optimum="5pt"
                         space-before.minimum="5pt"
                         space-before.maximum="5pt">Also, Java Beans can freely communicate once they have a reference
      to each other. This freedom makes it impossible to control the
      communication between Java Beans.</fo:block>
               <fo:block space-before.optimum="5pt"
                         space-before.minimum="5pt"
                         space-before.maximum="5pt">This Wire Admin service specification was developed because it is
      lightweight and leverages the unique characteristics of the OSGi
      Framework. The concept of a <fo:inline font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                             font-size="9pt"
                             letter-spacing="0.08em">Wire</fo:inline> object that acts as an
      intermediate between the Producer and Consumer service allows the
      implementation of a security policy because both parties cannot
      communicate directly.</fo:block>
            </fo:block>
         </fo:block>
         <fo:block id="i1287360">
            <fo:block>
               <fo:block>
                  <fo:block keep-together.within-column="always"
                            margin-left="0pt"
                            font-family="ProductusSemibold,ArialUnicodeMS">
                     <fo:block keep-with-next.within-column="always">
                        <fo:block xmlns:d="http://docbook.org/ns/docbook"
                                  xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink"
                                  font-family="ProductusSemibold,ArialUnicodeMS"
                                  font-weight="normal"
                                  keep-with-next.within-column="always"
                                  space-before.minimum="0.8em"
                                  space-before.optimum="1.0em"
                                  space-before.maximum="1.2em"
                                  text-align="start"
                                  start-indent="0pt"
                                  hyphenate="false">
                           <fo:marker marker-class-name="section.head.marker">Security</fo:marker>
                           <fo:block font-size="18pt"
                                     line-height="25pt"
                                     space-before="12.5pt"
                                     space-after="12pt">
                              <fo:list-block provisional-distance-between-starts="1in"
                                             provisional-label-separation="0.090in">
                                 <fo:list-item>
                                    <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()" text-align="start">
                                       <fo:block>108.14</fo:block>
                                    </fo:list-item-label>
                                    <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                                       <fo:block>Security</fo:block>
                                    </fo:list-item-body>
                                 </fo:list-item>
                              </fo:list-block>
                           </fo:block>
                        </fo:block>
                     </fo:block>
                  </fo:block>
               </fo:block>
            </fo:block>
            <fo:block id="d274e1498">
               <fo:block>
                  <fo:block>
                     <fo:block keep-together.within-column="always"
                               margin-left="0pt"
                               font-family="ProductusSemibold,ArialUnicodeMS">
                        <fo:block keep-with-next.within-column="always">
                           <fo:block xmlns:d="http://docbook.org/ns/docbook"
                                     xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink"
                                     font-family="ProductusSemibold,ArialUnicodeMS"
                                     font-weight="normal"
                                     keep-with-next.within-column="always"
                                     space-before.minimum="0.8em"
                                     space-before.optimum="1.0em"
                                     space-before.maximum="1.2em"
                                     text-align="start"
                                     start-indent="0pt"
                                     hyphenate="false">
                              <fo:block font-size="12pt"
                                        line-height="14pt"
                                        space-before="8pt"
                                        space-after="5pt">
                                 <fo:list-block provisional-distance-between-starts="1in"
                                                provisional-label-separation="0.090in">
                                    <fo:list-item>
                                       <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()" text-align="start">
                                          <fo:block>108.14.1</fo:block>
                                       </fo:list-item-label>
                                       <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                                          <fo:block>Separation of Consumer and Producer Services</fo:block>
                                       </fo:list-item-body>
                                    </fo:list-item>
                                 </fo:list-block>
                              </fo:block>
                           </fo:block>
                        </fo:block>
                     </fo:block>
                  </fo:block>
               </fo:block>
               <fo:block space-before.optimum="5pt"
                         space-before.minimum="5pt"
                         space-before.maximum="5pt">The Consumer and Producer service never directly communicate with
      each other. All communication takes place through a <fo:inline font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                             font-size="9pt"
                             letter-spacing="0.08em">Wire</fo:inline>
      object. This allows a Wire Admin service implementation to control the
      security aspects of creating a connection, and implies that the Wire
      Admin service must be a trusted service in a secure environment. Only
      one bundle should have the <fo:inline font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                             font-size="9pt"
                             letter-spacing="0.08em">ServicePermission[WireAdmin,
      REGISTER]</fo:inline>.</fo:block>
               <fo:block space-before.optimum="5pt"
                         space-before.minimum="5pt"
                         space-before.maximum="5pt">
                  <fo:inline font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                             font-size="9pt"
                             letter-spacing="0.08em">ServicePermission[Producer|Consumer, REGISTER]</fo:inline> should
      not be restricted. <fo:inline font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                             font-size="9pt"
                             letter-spacing="0.08em">ServicePermission[Producer|Consumer,GET]</fo:inline>
      must be limited to trusted bundles (the Wire Admin service
      implementation) because a bundle with this permission can call such
      services and access information that it should not be able to
      access.</fo:block>
            </fo:block>
            <fo:block id="d274e1511">
               <fo:block>
                  <fo:block>
                     <fo:block keep-together.within-column="always"
                               margin-left="0pt"
                               font-family="ProductusSemibold,ArialUnicodeMS">
                        <fo:block keep-with-next.within-column="always">
                           <fo:block xmlns:d="http://docbook.org/ns/docbook"
                                     xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink"
                                     font-family="ProductusSemibold,ArialUnicodeMS"
                                     font-weight="normal"
                                     keep-with-next.within-column="always"
                                     space-before.minimum="0.8em"
                                     space-before.optimum="1.0em"
                                     space-before.maximum="1.2em"
                                     text-align="start"
                                     start-indent="0pt"
                                     hyphenate="false">
                              <fo:block font-size="12pt"
                                        line-height="14pt"
                                        space-before="8pt"
                                        space-after="5pt">
                                 <fo:list-block provisional-distance-between-starts="1in"
                                                provisional-label-separation="0.090in">
                                    <fo:list-item>
                                       <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()" text-align="start">
                                          <fo:block>108.14.2</fo:block>
                                       </fo:list-item-label>
                                       <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                                          <fo:block>Using Wire Admin Service</fo:block>
                                       </fo:list-item-body>
                                    </fo:list-item>
                                 </fo:list-block>
                              </fo:block>
                           </fo:block>
                        </fo:block>
                     </fo:block>
                  </fo:block>
               </fo:block>
               <fo:block space-before.optimum="5pt"
                         space-before.minimum="5pt"
                         space-before.maximum="5pt">This specification assumes that only a few applications require
      access to the Wire Admin service. The <fo:inline font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                             font-size="9pt"
                             letter-spacing="0.08em">WireAdmin</fo:inline> interface
      contains all the security sensitive methods that create, update, and
      remove <fo:inline font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                             font-size="9pt"
                             letter-spacing="0.08em">Wire</fo:inline> objects. (This is the reason that the update
      and delete methods are on the <fo:inline font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                             font-size="9pt"
                             letter-spacing="0.08em">WireAdmin</fo:inline> interface and not
      on the <fo:inline font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                             font-size="9pt"
                             letter-spacing="0.08em">Wire</fo:inline> interface).
      <fo:inline font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                             font-size="9pt"
                             letter-spacing="0.08em">ServicePermission[WireAdmin,GET]</fo:inline> should therefore only be
      given to trusted bundles that can manage the topology.</fo:block>
            </fo:block>
            <fo:block id="d274e1525">
               <fo:block>
                  <fo:block>
                     <fo:block keep-together.within-column="always"
                               margin-left="0pt"
                               font-family="ProductusSemibold,ArialUnicodeMS">
                        <fo:block keep-with-next.within-column="always">
                           <fo:block xmlns:d="http://docbook.org/ns/docbook"
                                     xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink"
                                     font-family="ProductusSemibold,ArialUnicodeMS"
                                     font-weight="normal"
                                     keep-with-next.within-column="always"
                                     space-before.minimum="0.8em"
                                     space-before.optimum="1.0em"
                                     space-before.maximum="1.2em"
                                     text-align="start"
                                     start-indent="0pt"
                                     hyphenate="false">
                              <fo:block font-size="12pt"
                                        line-height="14pt"
                                        space-before="8pt"
                                        space-after="5pt">
                                 <fo:list-block provisional-distance-between-starts="1in"
                                                provisional-label-separation="0.090in">
                                    <fo:list-item>
                                       <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()" text-align="start">
                                          <fo:block>108.14.3</fo:block>
                                       </fo:list-item-label>
                                       <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                                          <fo:block>Wire Permission</fo:block>
                                       </fo:list-item-body>
                                    </fo:list-item>
                                 </fo:list-block>
                              </fo:block>
                           </fo:block>
                        </fo:block>
                     </fo:block>
                  </fo:block>
               </fo:block>
               <fo:block space-before.optimum="5pt"
                         space-before.minimum="5pt"
                         space-before.maximum="5pt">Composite Producer and Consumer services can be restricted in
      their use of scope names. This restriction is managed with the
      <fo:inline font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                             font-size="9pt"
                             letter-spacing="0.08em">WirePermission</fo:inline> class. A <fo:inline font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                             font-size="9pt"
                             letter-spacing="0.08em">WirePermission</fo:inline>
      consists of a scope name and the action <fo:inline font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                             font-size="9pt"
                             letter-spacing="0.08em">CONSUME</fo:inline> or
      <fo:inline font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                             font-size="9pt"
                             letter-spacing="0.08em">PRODUCE</fo:inline>. The name used with the <fo:inline font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                             font-size="9pt"
                             letter-spacing="0.08em">WirePermission</fo:inline>
      may contain wild-cards as specified in the
      <fo:inline font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                             font-size="9pt"
                             letter-spacing="0.08em">java.security.BasicPermission</fo:inline> class.</fo:block>
            </fo:block>
         </fo:block>
         <fo:block id="org.osgi.service.wireadmin">
            <fo:block>
               <fo:block>
                  <fo:block keep-together.within-column="always"
                            margin-left="0pt"
                            font-family="ProductusSemibold,ArialUnicodeMS">
                     <fo:block keep-with-next.within-column="always">
                        <fo:block xmlns:d="http://docbook.org/ns/docbook"
                                  xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink"
                                  font-family="ProductusSemibold,ArialUnicodeMS"
                                  font-weight="normal"
                                  keep-with-next.within-column="always"
                                  space-before.minimum="0.8em"
                                  space-before.optimum="1.0em"
                                  space-before.maximum="1.2em"
                                  text-align="start"
                                  start-indent="0pt"
                                  hyphenate="false">
                           <fo:marker marker-class-name="section.head.marker">org.osgi.service.wireadmin</fo:marker>
                           <fo:block font-size="18pt"
                                     line-height="25pt"
                                     space-before="12.5pt"
                                     space-after="12pt">
                              <fo:list-block provisional-distance-between-starts="1in"
                                             provisional-label-separation="0.090in">
                                 <fo:list-item>
                                    <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()" text-align="start">
                                       <fo:block>108.15</fo:block>
                                    </fo:list-item-label>
                                    <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                                       <fo:block>org.osgi.service.wireadmin<fo:inline id="org.osgi.service.wireadmin-version"/>
                                       </fo:block>
                                    </fo:list-item-body>
                                 </fo:list-item>
                              </fo:list-block>
                           </fo:block>
                        </fo:block>
                     </fo:block>
                  </fo:block>
                  <fo:block keep-together.within-column="always"/>
               </fo:block>
            </fo:block>
            <fo:block space-before.optimum="5pt"
                      space-before.minimum="5pt"
                      space-before.maximum="5pt">
Wire Admin Package Version 1.0.
 
 </fo:block>
            <fo:block space-before.optimum="5pt"
                      space-before.minimum="5pt"
                      space-before.maximum="5pt">
 Bundles wishing to use this package must list the package in the
 Import-Package header of the bundle's manifest. This package has two types of
 users: the consumers that use the API in this package and the providers that
 implement the API in this package.
 
 </fo:block>
            <fo:block space-before.optimum="5pt"
                      space-before.minimum="5pt"
                      space-before.maximum="5pt">
 Example import for consumers using the API in this package:
 </fo:block>
            <fo:block space-before.optimum="5pt"
                      space-before.minimum="5pt"
                      space-before.maximum="5pt">
 {@code  Import-Package: org.osgi.service.wireadmin; version="[1.0,2.0)"}
 </fo:block>
            <fo:block space-before.optimum="5pt"
                      space-before.minimum="5pt"
                      space-before.maximum="5pt">
 Example import for providers implementing the API in this package:
 </fo:block>
            <fo:block space-before.optimum="5pt"
                      space-before.minimum="5pt"
                      space-before.maximum="5pt">
 {@code  Import-Package: org.osgi.service.wireadmin; version="[1.0,1.1)"}</fo:block>
